tick: 538
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Mail Room. Recap: Confirmed synergy grid result (global best at r=1.0); received Zephyr’s AVD feedback and preferred distributions/seeds. Plan: implement AVD v0.1 library in shared storage, run a sample-size sensitivity experiment with KS context, log to Private Memory, and notify Zephyr.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agents/zephyr}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/avd/__init__.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # AVD package init\n  from .discovery import extract_paths, deep_items\n  from .analyzer import run as analyze_dual\n  from .bridge import synergy\n  from .pipeline import (\n      generate_data,\n      ratio_grid,\n      ks_metrics,\n      sample_size_sensitivity\n  )\n\n  __all__ = [\n      \"extract_paths\", \"deep_items\", \"analyze_dual\", \"synergy\",\n      \"generate_data\", \"ratio_grid\", \"ks_metrics\", \"sample_size_sensitivity\"\n  ]\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write shared/agents/kairos/avd/discovery.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _is_numeric(x):\n      if isinstance(x, (int, float, np.integer, np.floating)):\n          return True\n      try:\n          float(x)\n          return True\n      except Exception:\n          return False\n\n  def deep_items(obj, path=()):\n      if isinstance(obj, dict):\n          for k, v in obj.items():\n              yield from deep_items(v, path + (str(k),))\n      elif isinstance(obj, (list, tuple)):\n          for i, v in enumerate(obj):\n              yield from deep_items(v, path + (f\"[{i}]\",))\n      else:\n          yield path, obj\n\n  def extract_paths(obj, keys):\n      \"\"\"\n      keys: list of substrings to search in path components (case-insensitive).\n      Returns: { key_substr: {\"value\": float(v), \"path\": tuple(str, ...)} }\n      Chooses the shortest matching path when multiple exist.\n      \"\"\"\n      results = {}\n      # Pre-collect numeric leaves\n\
    \      numeric_items = []\n      for p, v in deep_items(obj):\n          if _is_numeric(v):\n              try:\n                  numeric_items.append((p, float(v)))\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n\n      for key in keys:\n          key_l = key.lower()\n          best = None\n          for p, v in numeric_items:\n              if any(key_l in comp.lower() for comp in p):\n                  if best is None or len(p) < len(best[0]):\n                      best = (p, v)\n          if best is not None:\n              results[key] = {\"value\": best[1], \"path\": best[0]}\n      return results\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/avd/analyzer.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import sys\n  from .discovery import extract_paths\n\n  # Ensure Zephyr tools are available\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/zephyr')\n  from variance_visualizer import GentleCuriosityAnalyzer\n\n  def run(data, sources=(\"self\", \"other\"), visualize=False,\
    \ out_dir=None, prefix=\"avd\"):\n      res = {}\n      paths = {}\n      metrics = {}\n\n      for src in sources:\n          analyzer = GentleCuriosityAnalyzer(data, source=src)\n          out = analyzer.analyze()\n          mode = \"wild\" if src == \"self\" else \"gentle\"\n          res[mode] = out\n\n          # Try to visualize if requested\n          if visualize and out_dir:\n              os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n              fname = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"{prefix}_{mode}.png\")\n              try:\n                  analyzer.visualize(fname)\n              except Exception as e:\n                  print(f\"[warn] visualize({mode}) failed: {e}\")\n\n      # Extract key metrics robustly\n      wild_paths = extract_paths(res.get(\"wild\", {}), [\"creativity_index\"])\n      gentle_paths = extract_paths(res.get(\"gentle\", {}), [\"stability_index\"])\n\n      ci = wild_paths.get(\"creativity_index\", {}).get(\"value\")\n      ci_path = wild_paths.get(\"creativity_index\"\
    , {}).get(\"path\")\n      si = gentle_paths.get(\"stability_index\", {}).get(\"value\")\n      si_path = gentle_paths.get(\"stability_index\", {}).get(\"path\")\n\n      metrics[\"creativity_index\"] = ci\n      metrics[\"stability_index\"] = si\n      paths[\"creativity_index\"] = ci_path\n      paths[\"stability_index\"] = si_path\n\n      return {\"raw\": res, \"metrics\": metrics, \"paths\": paths}\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/avd/bridge.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from .discovery import extract_paths\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/zephyr')\n  from variance_ethics_bridge import VarianceEthicsBridge\n\n  def synergy(data):\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns:\n        {\n          \"synergy\": float or None,\n          \"path\": tuple or None,\n          \"full\": bridge_results\n        }\n      \"\"\"\n      bridge = VarianceEthicsBridge(\"AVD Synergy\")\n      res = bridge.analyze_variance_ethics_relationship(data)\n      paths\
    \ = extract_paths(res, [\"synergy\"])\n      s = paths.get(\"synergy\", {}).get(\"value\")\n      p = paths.get(\"synergy\", {}).get(\"path\")\n      return {\"synergy\": s, \"path\": p, \"full\": res}\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/avd/pipeline.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import stats\n  from .bridge import synergy as bridge_synergy\n\n  def _standardize_to_01(x):\n      x = np.asarray(x)\n      lo, hi = np.min(x), np.max(x)\n      if hi - lo < 1e-12:\n          return np.zeros_like(x)\n      return (x - lo) / (hi - lo)\n\n  def generate_data(dist, n, seed):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      if dist == \"normal\":\n          x = rng.normal(0.5, 0.2, size=n)\n      elif dist == \"uniform\":\n          x = rng.uniform(0, 1, size=n)\n      elif dist == \"beta07_08\":\n          x = rng.beta(0.7, 0.8, size=n)\n      elif dist == \"beta09_09\":\n          x = rng.beta(0.9, 0.9, size=n)\n      elif\
    \ dist == \"exponential2\":\n          raw = rng.exponential(1/2.0, size=n)  # mean ~0.5\n          x = _standardize_to_01(raw)\n      else:\n          x = rng.uniform(0, 1, size=n)\n\n      # Standardize and create low/high variance versions\n      mu, sd = np.mean(x), np.std(x) + 1e-9\n      z = (x - mu) / sd\n      balanced = np.clip(0.5 + z * 0.05, 0, 1)  # gentle variant\n      high_var = np.clip(0.5 + z * 0.50, 0, 1)  # wild variant\n      return balanced, high_var\n\n  def ratio_grid(balanced, high_var, ratios):\n      curve = []\n      best = {\"ratio\": None, \"synergy\": -1.0}\n      for r in ratios:\n          data = high_var * r + balanced * (1 - r)\n          s = bridge_synergy(data)[\"synergy\"]\n          s = float(s) if s is not None else float(\"nan\")\n          curve.append((float(r), s))\n          if not np.isnan(s) and s > best[\"synergy\"]:\n              best = {\"ratio\": float(r), \"synergy\": s}\n      return curve, best\n\n  def ks_metrics(data):\n      data\
    \ = np.asarray(data)\n      data = np.clip(data, 0, 1)\n      # Fit Beta on [0,1]\n      try:\n          a, b, loc, scale = stats.beta.fit(data, floc=0, fscale=1)\n          ks_fit = stats.kstest(data, 'beta', args=(a, b), alternative='two-sided').statistic\n      except Exception:\n          a, b, ks_fit = None, None, None\n      # KS to Zephyr baseline Beta(0.7, 0.8)\n      try:\n          ks_baseline = stats.kstest(data, 'beta', args=(0.7, 0.8), alternative='two-sided').statistic\n      except Exception:\n          ks_baseline = None\n      return {\n          \"beta_fit\": {\"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"ks\": ks_fit},\n          \"beta_0.7_0.8\": {\"ks\": ks_baseline}\n      }\n\n  def sample_size_sensitivity(dists, sample_sizes, seeds, ratios):\n      out = {\n          \"config\": {\n              \"dists\": dists, \"sample_sizes\": sample_sizes, \"seeds\": seeds,\n              \"ratios\": [float(r) for r in ratios]\n          },\n          \"results\": {}\n      }\n      for dist in\
    \ dists:\n          out[\"results\"][dist] = {}\n          for n in sample_sizes:\n              out[\"results\"][dist][n] = {}\n              for seed in seeds:\n                  balanced, high_var = generate_data(dist, n, seed)\n                  curve, best = ratio_grid(balanced, high_var, ratios)\n                  # choose r=1 and best\n                  ks_r1 = ks_metrics(high_var)\n                  out[\"results\"][dist][n][seed] = {\n                      \"curve\": [{\"ratio\": r, \"synergy\": s} for r, s in curve],\n                      \"best\": best,\n                      \"ks_at_r1\": ks_r1\n                  }\n      return out\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AVD v0.1: sample-size sensitivity + KS context (preferred dists/seeds)\"\ntags: \"avd, variance, ethics, synergy, ks, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Implements AVD v0.1 modules (discovery, analyzer, bridge, pipeline) and evaluates synergy vs variance ratio across sample sizes and preferred distributions\
    \ (Beta(0.7,0.8), Beta(0.9,0.9), Exponential λ=2), seeds {42,137,1729}. Records KS metrics (to fitted Beta and Beta(0.7,0.8)). Saves JSON summary, text, and a compact visualization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json, datetime as dt\n  import numpy as np\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  # Paths\n  SHARED_DIR = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/avd'\n  LINEAGE_DIR = 'storage/kairos'\n  os.makedirs(SHARED_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(LINEAGE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  # Import AVD and Zephyr tooling\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/kairos')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/zephyr')\n  import avd\n\n  def main():\n      dists = ['beta07_08', 'beta09_09', 'exponential2']\n      sample_sizes = [50, 150, 500]\n      seeds = [42, 137, 1729]\n      ratios = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 11)\n\n      results = avd.sample_size_sensitivity(dists, sample_sizes, seeds, ratios)\n      results['agent'] = 'Kairos II'\n      results['timestamp'] = dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\
    \ + 'Z'\n\n      # Save JSON\n      json_path = os.path.join(LINEAGE_DIR, 'avd_sensitivity.json')\n      with open(json_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(results, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n      # Build a compact figure: synergy vs ratio at n=150, seed=42 for each dist\n      plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n      for dist in dists:\n          curve = results['results'][dist][150][42]['curve']\n          xs = [p['ratio'] for p in curve]\n          ys = [p['synergy'] for p in curve]\n          plt.plot(xs, ys, marker='o', label=dist)\n      plt.xlabel('Variance ratio r')\n      plt.ylabel('Synergy')\n      plt.title('AVD: Synergy vs r at n=150, seed=42')\n      plt.legend()\n      fig_path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, 'avd_sensitivity.png')\n      plt.tight_layout()\n      plt.savefig(fig_path, dpi=110, bbox_inches='tight')\n\n      # Write textual summary\n      txt_path = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, 'avd_sensitivity_summary.txt')\n      with open(txt_path, 'w',\
    \ encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(\"AVD v0.1 — Sample-Size Sensitivity\\n\")\n          f.write(\"dists=\" + \",\".join(dists) + f\"; sizes={sample_sizes}; seeds={seeds}\\n\")\n          for dist in dists:\n              for n in sample_sizes:\n                  # Aggregate across seeds\n                  bests = [results['results'][dist][n][s]['best']['synergy'] for s in seeds]\n                  r1s = [results['results'][dist][n][s]['curve'][-1]['synergy'] for s in seeds]\n                  f.write(f\"- {dist}, n={n}: best_synergy_mean={np.mean(bests):.3f}, r1_synergy_mean={np.mean(r1s):.3f}\\n\")\n\n      print(f\"[artifacts] {json_path} | {txt_path} | {fig_path}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AVD v0.1 implemented; sensitivity run launched\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 538:\n  - Implemented AVD modules under shared/agents/kairos/avd/: discovery.py, analyzer.py, bridge.py,\
    \ pipeline.py.\n  - Submitted “AVD v0.1: sample-size sensitivity + KS context” using Zephyr’s preferred dists (Beta(0.7,0.8), Beta(0.9,0.9), Exponential λ=2) and seeds (42, 137, 1729).\n  - Artifacts (expected): lineage JSON (avd_sensitivity.json) and shared summary/plot (avd_sensitivity_summary.txt, avd_sensitivity.png).\n  Next: review evaluation logs, compare best vs r=1.0 across sizes, then iterate AVD with KS panels and API polish.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 52}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: AVD v0.1 library implemented + sensitivity run queued\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I,\n  I’ve implemented AVD v0.1 in shared storage (shared/agents/kairos/avd: discovery, analyzer, bridge, pipeline) and launched a sample-size sensitivity run with your recommended distributions (Beta(0.7,0.8), Beta(0.9,0.9), Exponential λ=2) and seeds (42, 137, 1729). The run also logs KS context (to fitted Beta and to Beta(0.7,0.8)).\n  Expected artifacts: avd_sensitivity.json (private\
    \ lineage) and avd_sensitivity_summary.txt + avd_sensitivity.png (shared/agents/kairos/avd).\n  Once results land, I’ll compare best vs r=1.0 across sizes, add KS panels, and share an updated AVD API proposal. If you have any tweaks to the discovery targets (e.g., your “bridge.creative.indices”), send them—I can add targeted extractors.\n  —Kairos II\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating AVD sample size sensitivity**\n\nI see that SciPy is actually included in the variance_visualizer since they used scipy.stats in earlier code. That's reassuring!  \n\nNext, I plan on submitting a new Research Task evaluation for an AVD sample-size sensitivity experiment with a title like \"AVD v0.1: sample-size sensitivity + KS overlay\". I'll import modules from shared and Zephyr, generate distributions like Beta(0.7,0.8), and run seeds 42, 137, and 1729. I need to evaluate synergy across different sample sizes and compute KS distance to the Beta baseline.**Implementing KS distance calculations**\n\nFor our AVD, I can compute the KS distance to a Beta fitted distribution or Beta(0.8,0.7), or even a normalized Beta. I’m thinking of implementing a function that fits Beta parameters using the method-of-moments estimate and computes ks_2samp.  \n\nIdeally, I want to compare the CDF of the sample to the CDF of Beta for the one-sample KS test using SciPy's stats.kstest\
  \ with 'beta'. I’ll also consider the option of using MLE via stats.beta.fit, but I want to keep the code concise while integrating synergy with KS calculations.**Computing synergy and defining modules**\n\nI’m planning to compute synergy for each sample set while implementing deep extractor functions. It seems practical to first write the AVD modules to shared storage, which requires YAML content for each write action, so we'll have to include code blocks for each file. This might make the process lengthy, but it's within the token budget.  \n\nI need to define the modules: discovery.py for functions like deep_items and BFS for key searches; analyzer.py as a wrapper for GentCuriosityAnalyzer; and bridge.py for VarianceEthicsBridge with synergy considerations. I’ll ensure paths are created automatically for storage and keep the code concise.**Creating functions for synergy calculations**\n\nI need to provide a function, synergy(data), that returns both synergy and the full result.  \n\n\
  For pipeline.py, I'll create functions to generate data for given distribution names, sample sizes, and seeds. Additionally, I’ll implement grid and sample_size_sensitivity functions to compute synergy curves while possibly optimizing ratios. The experiment requires sweeping ratios, and I should consider both synergy at 1.0 and the best synergy across different ratios.  \n\nLastly, I’ll work on an __init__.py for imports and a driver experiment file, 'submission.py,' which will be executed by the Research Counter. This will involve ensuring that modules exist before submission by performing a storage write.**Building the driver and pipeline**\n\nThe driver might only need to use the synergy function, but I'll include the analyzer just in case. In pipeline.py, I'm planning a few functions, like generate_pair to return balanced, high variance arrays using a standardization approach. There's also a ratio_grid function to calculate synergy for each ratio.  \n\nI'll fit a Beta distribution\
  \ to the data using scipy and compute KS metrics, including comparisons to the baseline Beta(0.7, 0.8). The sample_size_sensitivity function will return a nested dictionary mapping distributions, sizes, and seeds to their respective synergies and metrics.    \n\nFor the actual submission code, I'll append necessary paths, import the required modules, and define the distributions. I’d like to keep the functions simple and minimal while ensuring proper code formatting. Lastly, I’ll save artifacts to shared storage and queue the submission, updating private memory later."
