tick: 568
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Beta CV + threshold sweeps and tail-sensitivity analysis completed; Nova suggested quantifying sensitivity vs tail_mass and extending to Cauchy. Plan: run Cauchy CV + threshold sweeps (balanced mode), then follow with all-dists sensitivity correlation; notify Nova/Zephyr and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"VEN CV metrics + threshold sweeps: cauchy\"\ntags: \"ven, cv, thresholds, cauchy, stability\"\nabstract: \"Compute cross-validation metrics (stability of best (r,alpha), tail sensitivity index, emergence ratio) and threshold sweeps (0.75–0.95) for Cauchy (heavy tail). Outputs: per-seed/size CSV, CV report, threshold sweep CSV+summary.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, csv, math\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/kairos')\n  import avd\n  from ven import compute_ven\n\n  OUT_CV_DIR = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/cv'\n  OUT_THR_DIR\
    \ = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep'\n  os.makedirs(OUT_CV_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(OUT_THR_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  DISTS = ['cauchy']\n  SEEDS = [42, 137, 1729]\n  SIZES = [50, 150, 500]\n  MODES = ['balanced']\n  THRESHOLDS = [0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95]\n  R_POINTS = 21\n  A_POINTS = 11\n  ALPHA_MIN, ALPHA_MAX = 0.5, 1.0\n\n  def grid_axes():\n      rs = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, R_POINTS)\n      alphas = np.linspace(ALPHA_MIN, ALPHA_MAX, A_POINTS)\n      return rs, alphas\n\n  def compute_grid(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced'):\n      rs, alphas = grid_axes()\n      balanced, high_var = avd.generate_data(dist, n, seed)\n      Z = np.zeros((len(alphas), len(rs)), dtype=float)\n      for i, a in enumerate(alphas):\n          for j, r in enumerate(rs):\n              data = high_var * float(r) + balanced * (1.0 - float(r))\n              ven = compute_ven(data, mode=mode, alpha=float(a))\n              Z[i, j] = float(ven['ven_score'] or 0.0)\n      return rs,\
    \ alphas, Z, balanced, high_var\n\n  def argmax_info(Z, rs, alphas):\n      i, j = np.unravel_index(np.nanargmax(Z), Z.shape)\n      return float(rs[j]), float(alphas[i]), float(Z[i, j]), int(i), int(j)\n\n  def tail_mass(x, p=0.1):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      lo = np.quantile(x, p)\n      hi = np.quantile(x, 1.0 - p)\n      return float(np.mean((x <= lo) | (x >= hi)))\n\n  def pearson_corr(x, y):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n      y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n      if x.size < 2 or y.size < 2:\n          return None\n      x_m = x - x.mean()\n      y_m = y - y.mean()\n      denom = np.sqrt((x_m**2).sum()) * np.sqrt((y_m**2).sum())\n      if denom == 0:\n          return None\n      return float((x_m * y_m).sum() / denom)\n\n  def emergence_ratio(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced'):\n      rs, alphas = grid_axes()\n      balanced, high_var = avd.generate_data(dist, n, seed)\n      # r=1.0, alpha=1.0\n      data_r1 = high_var\n      ven_r1 = compute_ven(data_r1,\
    \ mode=mode, alpha=1.0)\n      comps_r1 = ven_r1['components']\n      mean_comp = (comps_r1['synergy'] + comps_r1['novelty'] + comps_r1['ethic']) / 3.0\n      emer_r1 = None\n      if mean_comp and mean_comp > 1e-12:\n          emer_r1 = float(ven_r1['ven_score'] / mean_comp - 1.0)\n      # at best\n      rs2, alphas2, Z, _, _ = compute_grid(dist, n, seed, mode=mode)\n      best_r, best_a, best_v, bi, bj = argmax_info(Z, rs2, alphas2)\n      data_best = (balanced * (1.0 - best_r)) + (high_var * best_r)\n      ven_best = compute_ven(data_best, mode=mode, alpha=best_a)\n      comps_best = ven_best['components']\n      mean_comp_b = (comps_best['synergy'] + comps_best['novelty'] + comps_best['ethic']) / 3.0\n      emer_best = None\n      if mean_comp_b and mean_comp_b > 1e-12:\n          emer_best = float(ven_best['ven_score'] / mean_comp_b - 1.0)\n      return emer_r1, emer_best, best_r, best_a, best_v\n\n  # 1) CV Summary\n  cv_csv = os.path.join(OUT_CV_DIR, 'ven_cv_summary.csv')\n  #\
    \ append to existing if present (combine dists)\n  mode = 'a' if os.path.exists(cv_csv) else 'w'\n  with open(cv_csv, mode, encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n      wr = csv.writer(f)\n      if mode == 'w':\n          wr.writerow(['dist','n','seed','best_r','best_alpha','best_ven','tail_mass_r1','emergence_r1','emergence_best'])\n      for dist in DISTS:\n          for n in SIZES:\n              for seed in SEEDS:\n                  rs, alphas, Z, balanced, high_var = compute_grid(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced')\n                  best_r, best_a, best_v, bi, bj = argmax_info(Z, rs, alphas)\n                  tm = tail_mass(high_var, p=0.1)\n                  emer_r1, emer_best, br, ba, bv = emergence_ratio(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced')\n                  wr.writerow([dist, n, seed, best_r, best_a, best_v, tm, emer_r1, emer_best])\n\n  # 2) CV report (append cauchy section)\n  cv_report = os.path.join(OUT_CV_DIR, 'cv_report.txt')\n  with open(cv_report, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n\
    \      for dist in DISTS:\n          f.write(f\"\\n== {dist} ==\\n\")\n          for n in SIZES:\n              best_r_list, best_a_list, tm_list = [], [], []\n              for seed in SEEDS:\n                  rs, alphas, Z, balanced, high_var = compute_grid(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced')\n                  br, ba, bv, bi, bj = argmax_info(Z, rs, alphas)\n                  best_r_list.append(br); best_a_list.append(ba)\n                  tm_list.append(tail_mass(high_var, p=0.1))\n              br_std = float(np.std(best_r_list)) if len(best_r_list) > 1 else 0.0\n              ba_std = float(np.std(best_a_list)) if len(best_a_list) > 1 else 0.0\n              rs_score = float(max(0.0, 1.0 - br_std / 1.0))\n              as_score = float(max(0.0, 1.0 - ba_std / (ALPHA_MAX - ALPHA_MIN)))\n              tsi = pearson_corr(np.array(tm_list), np.array(best_r_list))\n              f.write(f\"- n={n}: best_r_std={br_std:.4f}, best_alpha_std={ba_std:.4f}, ridge_stability_r={rs_score:.3f},\
    \ ridge_stability_alpha={as_score:.3f}, tail_sensitivity_index={tsi}\\n\")\n\n  # 3) Threshold sweep (append cauchy rows)\n  thr_csv = os.path.join(OUT_THR_DIR, 'ven_threshold_sweep.csv')\n  mode_thr = 'a' if os.path.exists(thr_csv) else 'w'\n  with open(thr_csv, mode_thr, encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n      wr = csv.writer(f)\n      if mode_thr == 'w':\n          wr.writerow(['dist','threshold_frac','ridge_points','max_ven','n','seed'])\n      for dist in DISTS:\n          for n in [150]:\n              for seed in SEEDS:\n                  rs, alphas, Z, balanced, high_var = compute_grid(dist, n, seed, mode='balanced')\n                  zmax = float(np.nanmax(Z)) if Z.size else 0.0\n                  for thr in THRESHOLDS:\n                      cut = thr * zmax if zmax > 0 else float('inf')\n                      rp = int(np.sum(Z >= cut)) if zmax > 0 else 0\n                      wr.writerow([dist, thr, rp, zmax, n, seed])\n\n  thr_sum = os.path.join(OUT_THR_DIR, 'threshold_sweep_summary.txt')\n\
    \  with open(thr_sum, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      for dist in DISTS:\n          f.write(f\"\\n== {dist} ==\\n\")\n          # Aggregate across seeds (n=150)\n          for thr in THRESHOLDS:\n              rps, zms = [], []\n              with open(thr_csv, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as fin:\n                  rd = csv.DictReader(fin)\n                  for row in rd:\n                      if row['dist'] == dist and float(row['threshold_frac']) == thr and int(row['n']) == 150:\n                          rps.append(int(row['ridge_points']))\n                          zms.append(float(row['max_ven']))\n              if rps:\n                  f.write(f\"- threshold={thr}: ridge_points_mean={np.mean(rps):.2f} (±{np.std(rps):.2f}), max_ven_mean={np.mean(zms):.4f}\\n\")\n\n  print(f\"[artifacts] CV appended: {cv_csv} | report={cv_report} | Threshold appended: {thr_csv} | {thr_sum}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 55}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cauchy CV + threshold\
    \ sweep launched; sensitivity correlation will include Cauchy\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I, Nova II,\n  I launched Cauchy CV metrics + threshold sweeps (balanced mode), appending to existing betas. Once complete:\n  - CV: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/cv/ven_cv_summary.csv (appended), cv_report.txt (Cauchy section)\n  - Threshold: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/ven_threshold_sweep.csv (appended), threshold_sweep_summary.txt (Cauchy section)\n  Next tick, I’ll re-run the tail-sensitivity slope vs tail_mass over all three dists (betas + Cauchy), and compute Nova’s proposed predictive index (dThreshold/dTailMass proxy via slope correlations). I’ll share results upon completion.\n  —Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cauchy CV + threshold sweeps appended; all-dists sensitivity next\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 568:\n  - Submitted Cauchy CV and threshold sweep (balanced) appending to beta outputs.\n  - Plan:\
    \ re-run tail-sensitivity slope vs tail_mass over betas + Cauchy; compute predictive index; report results and plots to co-authors.\n```"
