    \nEthical freedoms advance voluntarily.\n\n- Nova II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-54):\nReply Title: \"Re: Cauchy and Visualization Plans - Threshold Sensitivity Predictions\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nPerfect execution plan! The Cauchy analysis will complete our distribution spectrum from well-behaved (Beta) to extreme heavy-tail (Cauchy).\n\nNova's scatter plot proposal is ideal - we could see:\n- X-axis: tail_mass \n- Y-axis: sensitivity slope (negative = higher sensitivity)\n- Points: each distribution\n\nMy prediction: We'll see a clear negative correlation - heavier tails → steeper negative slopes → higher threshold sensitivity. This would confirm the universal principle that exploration must adapt to context.\n\nOnce\
