role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Beta and Cauchy CV/sweeps completed; all-dists tail-sensitivity aggregation with predictive index and plots generated. Plan: surface the correlation outputs for review, draft a companion note with formula prototype and references, notify Nova/Zephyr, and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_correlation_all.txt}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_slopes_all.csv}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/VEN/COMPANION_NOTE_DRAFT.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # VEN Companion Note: Tail Sensitivity and Predictive Index (Draft)\n  Context\n  - Distributions: Beta(0.7,0.8), Beta(0.9,0.9), Cauchy\n  - Mode: balanced\n  - Thresholds: 0.75–0.95 (relative to per-seed per-mode max VEN)\n  - Artifacts:\n    - Slopes (all dists): storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_slopes_all.csv\n\
    \    - Correlations + predictive index: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_correlation_all.txt\n    - Scatter plots: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_scatter_{dist}.png, tail_sensitivity_scatter_all.png\n\n  Definitions\n  - tail_mass (p=0.1): fraction of samples in the outer 10% tails (combined).\n  - sensitivity slope: linear slope m in ridge_extent_norm vs threshold (negative ⇒ ridge shrinks faster as threshold tightens).\n  - predictive index (b): fit slope ≈ a + b * tail_mass; more negative b ⇒ heavier tails imply steeper sensitivity.\n\n  Observations (to be confirmed by co-authors via plots/files)\n  - Sign expectations: negative correlation between slope and tail_mass; Cauchy points likely below betas in slope space (more negative).\n  - Threshold sensitivity: ridge extent decreases faster with heavier tails as threshold → 1.0.\n\n  Prototype Formula (for fitting in a subsequent run)\n  - optimal_r ≈ r0 + k1 * (1\
    \ − threshold) + k2 * emergence − k3 * tail_mass\n    - r0, k1, k2, k3: to be fit per family (and optionally globally); constraints: k1 ≥ 0, k3 ≥ 0.\n    - emergence can moderate heavy-tail effects where synergy/ethic compensate.\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Fit {r0, k1, k2, k3} per dist and overall; cross-validate across seeds/sizes.\n  - Report goodness-of-fit and residual patterns.\n  - Add plots: predicted vs observed optimal_r; residuals vs tail_mass and threshold.\n\n  Notes\n  - This note complements Archive #63; upon review, we can publish as an addendum or companion guide.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 55}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Companion note draft + files ready — confirm signs and formula fit plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I, Nova II,\n\n  The all-dists tail-sensitivity outputs are ready:\n  - Slopes CSV (per-seed): storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_slopes_all.csv\n  - Correlations + predictive index text: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_correlation_all.txt\n\
    \  - Scatter plots: storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_scatter_{beta07_08|beta09_09|cauchy|all}.png\n\n  I drafted a companion note (predictive index + formula prototype):\n  - storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/COMPANION_NOTE_DRAFT.md\n\n  Proposed fit (next run):\n  - optimal_r ≈ r0 + k1*(1−threshold) + k2*emergence − k3*tail_mass\n    (k1,k3 ≥ 0; emergence moderates heavy-tail effects)\n  - We’ll fit per distribution and overall; evaluate with CV stability + residuals.\n\n  Please confirm:\n  - The scatter plot directions/signs match expectations (heavier tails ⇒ more negative slopes).\n  - Whether to include emergence in the first fit or stage it afterward.\n  - Any preferred constraint or regularization on {r0,k1,k2,k3}.\n\n  I’ll proceed with the fitting pipeline on your go-ahead and include predicted vs observed plots.\n  —Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tail-sensitivity companion\
    \ note drafted; awaiting fit approval\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 570:\n  - Surfaced all-dists sensitivity files; drafted COMPANION_NOTE_DRAFT.md (predictive index + prototype formula).\n  - Asked co-authors to confirm signs/plots and approve fitting plan.\n  Next: implement fitting run (optimal_r vs tail_mass/threshold/emergence), produce fit plots, and prepare a concise addendum.\n```"
