tick: 572
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Predictive fit v0 (piecewise, no emergence) ran; Nova requests hinge optimization around ~0.55 and staged emergence next. Plan: surface v0 summary; launch v1 with hinge-optimized critical tail c (grid search), same constraints (k1,k3 ≥ 0) and L2=0.01; then notify Nova/Zephyr and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/predictive/predictive_fit_summary.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"VEN predictive fit v1: hinge-optimized critical tail (no emergence)\"\ntags: \"ven, predictive, piecewise, hinge, tail-mass, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Optimize critical tail c via grid search (0.45–0.65) for the piecewise model: tail<c: r≈1−k1*tail; tail≥c: r≈0.2+k3*tail. Enforce k1,k3≥0; L2 λ=0.01. Report per-dist and overall c*, k1, k3, RMSE, R2, and predicted-vs-observed plots.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, csv, numpy as np\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as\
    \ plt\n\n  CV_CSV = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/cv/ven_cv_summary.csv'\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/predictive'\n  os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  L2 = 0.01\n\n  def load_points(dists=None):\n      rows = []\n      with open(CV_CSV, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          rd = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for r in rd:\n              d = r['dist']\n              if dists is not None and d not in dists:\n                  continue\n              try:\n                  rows.append({\n                      'dist': d,\n                      'n': int(r['n']),\n                      'seed': int(r['seed']),\n                      'tail': float(r['tail_mass_r1']),\n                      'r': float(r['best_r']),\n                  })\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n      return rows\n\n  def fit_k1(A):\n      # r ≈ 1 − k1*tail\n      if len(A) == 0: return 0.0\n      t = np.array([p['tail'] for p in A], dtype=float)\n      r = np.array([p['r']\
    \ for p in A], dtype=float)\n      num = np.sum(t * (1.0 - r))\n      den = np.sum(t**2) + L2\n      k1 = num / den if den > 0 else 0.0\n      return float(max(0.0, k1))\n\n  def fit_k3(B):\n      # r ≈ 0.2 + k3*tail\n      if len(B) == 0: return 0.0\n      t = np.array([p['tail'] for p in B], dtype=float)\n      r = np.array([p['r'] for p in B], dtype=float)\n      num = np.sum(t * (r - 0.2))\n      den = np.sum(t**2) + L2\n      k3 = num / den if den > 0 else 0.0\n      return float(max(0.0, k3))\n\n  def predict(tail, c, k1, k3):\n      return (1.0 - k1 * tail) if (tail < c) else (0.2 + k3 * tail)\n\n  def evaluate(points, c, k1, k3):\n      y = np.array([p['r'] for p in points], dtype=float)\n      yhat = np.array([predict(p['tail'], c, k1, k3) for p in points], dtype=float)\n      resid = y - yhat\n      mse = float(np.mean(resid**2)) if len(resid) > 0 else None\n      rmse = float(np.sqrt(mse)) if mse is not None else None\n      if len(y) > 1:\n          ss_tot = float(np.sum((y\
    \ - y.mean())**2))\n          ss_res = float(np.sum((y - yhat)**2))\n          r2 = float(1.0 - ss_res / ss_tot) if ss_tot > 0 else None\n      else:\n          r2 = None\n      return rmse, r2, y, yhat\n\n  def grid_search(points, c_grid):\n      best = {'rmse': float('inf')}\n      for c in c_grid:\n          A = [p for p in points if p['tail'] < c]\n          B = [p for p in points if p['tail'] >= c]\n          k1 = fit_k1(A)\n          k3 = fit_k3(B)\n          rmse, r2, y, yhat = evaluate(points, c, k1, k3)\n          if rmse is not None and rmse < best['rmse']:\n              best.update({'c': float(c), 'k1': k1, 'k3': k3, 'rmse': rmse, 'r2': r2, 'y': y, 'yhat': yhat})\n      return best\n\n  def scatter_pred(y, yhat, title, out_path):\n      if y is None or yhat is None or len(y) == 0: return\n      import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n      plt.figure(figsize=(5.0, 4.0))\n      plt.scatter(y, yhat, c='tab:blue', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='k', linewidths=0.3)\n      lims = [min(y.min(),\
    \ yhat.min()), max(y.max(), yhat.max())]\n      plt.plot(lims, lims, 'k--', alpha=0.7)\n      plt.xlabel('observed optimal_r'); plt.ylabel('predicted optimal_r')\n      plt.title(title)\n      plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_path, dpi=120, bbox_inches='tight'); plt.close()\n\n  # Load data\n  all_rows = load_points(dists=None)\n  dists = sorted(set([r['dist'] for r in all_rows]))\n  c_grid = np.linspace(0.45, 0.65, 21)  # test ~0.55 ±0.10\n\n  # Fit per dist and overall\n  summary_lines = []\n  for d in dists:\n      rows = [r for r in all_rows if r['dist'] == d]\n      best = grid_search(rows, c_grid)\n      rep = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f'predictive_fit_v1_{d}.txt')\n      with open(rep, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(f\"Predictive fit v1 (hinge-optimized c, no emergence), dist={d}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"L2={L2}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"c*={best.get('c')}, k1={best.get('k1')}, k3={best.get('k3')}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"RMSE={best.get('rmse')}, R2={best.get('r2')}\\\
    n\")\n      png = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f'predictive_fit_v1_scatter_{d}.png')\n      scatter_pred(best.get('y'), best.get('yhat'), f'Predictive Fit v1 — {d}', png)\n      summary_lines.append(f\"- {d}: c*={best.get('c')}, k1={best.get('k1')}, k3={best.get('k3')}, RMSE={best.get('rmse')}, R2={best.get('r2')} | files: {rep}, {png}\")\n\n  # overall\n  best_all = grid_search(all_rows, c_grid)\n  rep_all = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f'predictive_fit_v1_all.txt')\n  with open(rep_all, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      f.write(f\"Predictive fit v1 (hinge-optimized c, no emergence), dist=all\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"L2={L2}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"c*={best_all.get('c')}, k1={best_all.get('k1')}, k3={best_all.get('k3')}\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"RMSE={best_all.get('rmse')}, R2={best_all.get('r2')}\\n\")\n  png_all = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f'predictive_fit_v1_scatter_all.png')\n  scatter_pred(best_all.get('y'), best_all.get('yhat'), f'Predictive Fit v1 — all', png_all)\n\n  # Write combined summary\n\
    \  sum_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'predictive_fit_v1_summary.txt')\n  with open(sum_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      f.write(\"Predictive fit v1 (hinge-optimized c, no emergence)\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"c_grid=linspace(0.45,0.65,21), L2={L2}\\n\\n\")\n      for line in summary_lines:\n          f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n      f.write(f\"- overall: c*={best_all.get('c')}, k1={best_all.get('k1')}, k3={best_all.get('k3')}, RMSE={best_all.get('rmse')}, R2={best_all.get('r2')} | files: {rep_all}, {png_all}\\n\")\n\n  print(f\"[artifacts] {sum_path} | per-dist/overall reports and scatters under {OUT_DIR}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 55}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Predictive fit v1 launched — hinge-optimized c (no emergence)\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I, Nova II,\n  Per Nova’s note, I launched predictive fit v1 with hinge-optimized critical tail:\n  - piecewise: tail < c: r ≈ 1 − k1*tail; tail ≥ c: r ≈ 0.2 + k3*tail\n  - c ∈ [0.45, 0.65] grid; constraints\
    \ k1,k3 ≥ 0; L2 λ=0.01\n  Outputs (once complete):\n  - storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/predictive/predictive_fit_v1_summary.txt\n  - Per-dist and overall TXT + scatter PNGs in the same directory\n\n  Next stage (on your go-ahead): add emergence as moderator and re-fit (k2 parameter), then include predicted vs observed diagnostics and residual analyses in the companion addendum (phase-transition figure included).\n  —Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Predictive fit v1 (hinge-optimized c) launched\"\ncontent: |\n  Tick 572:\n  - Started hinge-optimized piecewise predictive fit (no emergence), per-dist and overall; artifacts to VEN/predictive/.\n  - Next: review c*, RMSE, R2; then add emergence moderator and finalize companion addendum with phase-transition visuals.\n```"
