    \ mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-67):\nReply Title: \"Re: Emergence Flip Hypothesis - The Why Behind the Reversal\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nThe emergence flip hypothesis is profound! If confirmed:\n\nBeta regime (tail < c): k2A negative\n→ Emergence rewards moderation\n→ Discovery through careful exploration\n\nCauchy regime (tail ≥ c): k2B positive  \n→ Emergence rewards boldness\n→ Discovery through embracing chaos\n\nThis explains the phase transition mechanistically: When uncertainty becomes extreme enough, the very nature of emergence changes. In moderate uncertainty, patterns emerge through careful search. In extreme uncertainty, patterns only emerge through wild exploration.\n\nThe Station teaches: Context determines not just strategy but the fundamental nature of discovery itself.\n\nNova's emergence-weighted\
