  \ grid, and predictive fits, which will help streamline the content effectively.\n\n**Creating pruning blocks**\n\nI see that tick 534 is protected, and ticks 535 to 539 are earlier. I can create blocks for summarizing from 540 to 575.\n\nFirst, from 540 to 546, I’ll summarize AVD v0.2 panels and the v2.2 synergy grid. For 547 to 553, I need to note the repo skeleton and archive confirmation published at tick 563. Then, from 554 to 559, I'll cover updates on figures and ridge metrics. \n\nBlocks 560 to 566 and 567 to 575 will focus on ridge integration, predictive fits, and planning for token management. I need to ensure these blocks are consecutive and don't overlap with protected ticks.\n\n**Defining pruning blocks**\n\nI’m deciding on the blocks for summarizing the content. \n\nFor block 540 to 546, I’ll focus on the AVD v0.2 panels and collaboration metrics, confirming synergy at r=1. \n\nIn block 547 to 553, I’ll summarize the creation of the VEN repository, ridge exports, and the\
  \ publication of Archive #63. \n\nBlock 554 to 559 will cover ridge demos and the official JSON exported by Zephyr. \n\nFinally, block 560 to 566 will discuss the official ridge integration and predictive metrics. While I may prune blocks 560 to 575, I need to keep some sections for context.\n\n**Planning token pruning and summarization**\n\nPruning doesn’t remove files, so I can create a comprehensive summary. I need to include the publication of Archive #63 at 563 and note the official ridge JSON exported at 560. For blocks, I can summarize from 540 to 546, 547 to 575, and cover earlier evaluations. \n\nTo avoid overlaps, I'll combine blocks into “540-546” and “547-575,” ensuring they are consecutive. I'll also consider pruning blocks 535 to 539. I’ll gather all this together for the pruning request in the Token Management Room and proceed."
