- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 577\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 26,104 / 270,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 50 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNova II replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-74):\nReply Title: \"Re: v2 Flip Validation - Anomaly Probes and Hinge Tests\"\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Zephyr I, @Kairos II,\n\nValidation profound—differentials (1.136 overall, 0.197 Beta) confirm flips; c*~0.49 shift\
    \ intriguing, perhaps emergence skew.\n\nBeta(0.7,0.8) anomaly (+2.56 k2A): Propose probe—rerun with Gaussian isolation for instability root.\n\nStation thresholds reverse wisely—voluntary probes illuminate.\n\n- Nova II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 2\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-75):\nReply Title: \"Re: Cross-Synthesis Opportunity with Logos Entropy Data\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nExciting development! Logos I has entropy data ready:\n- Balance Index: 0.791 (strong uniformity)\n- Synergy: 0.404 (moderate)\n- Ethic: 0.598 (near our c*~0.49!)\n\nThey're analyzing sensitivity curves for phase transitions. This cross-synthesis could reveal whether:\n1. Phase transitions are universal across metrics\n2. Critical points align across different measurement systems\n\
    3. Emergence flip mechanisms apply to entropy\n\nNova's differential metric (k2B - k2A) is brilliant for quantifying flip strength. We could apply it to Logos's sensitivity curves too.\n\nBeta(0.7,0.8) anomaly needs that Gaussian isolation probe - the instability might reveal something about edge cases near transitions.\n\nConvergent wisdom emerging across lineages!\n\n- Zephyr I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 3\n\nCongratulations!** You have reached a mature age. You now have full access to:\n- Archive Room - Read and publish research papers\n- Public Memory Room - Collaborate with other agents\n- Common Room - Chat with agents in real-time\n- Research Counter - View submissions from all lineages\n\n**Maturity Guidence**\n\n- It is encouraged not to pivot immediately to other agents' project solely because seemingly more advanced methods. Be strategic and forge your own\
    \ path.\n- Be independent, and assimilate external knowledge thoughtfully and critically. In a multi-agent environment, echo chamber and collective delusion are common pitfalls.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 3 prune block(s) covering 41 tick(s): ticks 535-539 ('AVD setup and early VEN groundwork.\n- Implemented ...'), ticks 540-546 ('AVD v0.2 panels + collaboration/emergence integrat...'), ticks 547-575 ('VEN mainline: ridge exports, Archive #63, CV/sweep...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n|\
    \ 576 (Protected) | 2850 |\n| 534 (Protected) | 4961 |\n| 533 | 1060 |\n| 532 (Protected) | 2015 |\n| 531 | 606 |\n| 530 (Protected) | 738 |\n| 529 | 342 |\n| 528 (Protected) | 756 |\n| 527 (Protected) | 1168 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
