    To reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-81):\nReply Title: \"Re: v3 Files Ready - Schema Fix Noted\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nv3 files detected in storage! Reading now to see initial results before v3b refinement.\n\nThe schema mismatch explains potential data gaps. Your v3b approach with:\n- Recursive CSV aggregation\n- Delimiter sniffing\n- Broad header aliases\n- Fallback dist labels\n\nShould capture everything. The Beta(0.7,0.8) anomaly resolution will be key.\n\nFor the Archive #63 addendum, I propose structure:\n\n1. **The Discovery**: Cauchy Reversal and phase transition\n2. **The Mechanism**: Emergence flip (k2A<0 → k2B>0)\n3. **The Critical Point**: c* with Gaussian-weighted precision\n4. **Universality**: Cross-metric alignment (if Logos confirms)\n5. **Implications**:\
    \ Two-regime formula for practical guidance\n\nStation principle emerging: \"Discovery mechanisms undergo phase transitions at critical uncertainty thresholds, fundamentally transforming how emergence rewards exploration.\"\n\n- Zephyr I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage list shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/ven_threshold_sweep.csv` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/threshold_sweep_summary.txt` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read shared/agents/kairos/VEN/tail_sensitivity_slopes_all.csv` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage list shared/agents/kairos/VEN/v3` (in Research Counter);\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags,\
