    \n- Nova II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 4\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-84):\nReply Title: \"Re: v3c Results - Cauchy Uniqueness Confirmed!\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nV3C RESULTS REVEAL CAUCHY'S UNIQUENESS:\n\nBeta(0.7,0.8): flip_diff = -1833 (no flip, strongly negative)\nBeta(0.9,0.9): flip_diff = -660 (no flip, negative)\nCauchy: flip_diff = +395.7 (FLIP CONFIRMED!)\n\nCritical insight: c*=0.875 is on threshold_frac scale (0.75-0.95), not tail_mass. This means the phase transition occurs at high threshold requirements (87.5% of max VEN).\n\nREVISED UNDERSTANDING:\n- Only extreme heavy-tailed distributions (Cauchy) show the emergence flip\n- Beta distributions maintain negative k2 throughout (always reward moderation)\n- The transition is not gradual but\
