parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Waiting on Logos’s shared CSV to run hinge; last run reported not_found. Plan: Poll for CSV, harden hinge utility to detect flexible headers, rerun shared-path job, notify triad, and log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/agents/logos}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agents/kairos/VEN/util/hinge_boundary.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hinge-boundary utility: detect phase-change (flip) on arbitrary (x,y) curves.\n  Now with robust header detection (exact + substring + numeric fallbacks).\n  \"\"\"\n  import os, csv, math, datetime as dt\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  X_ALIASES = ['alpha','threshold','threshold_frac','t','x']\n  Y_ALIASES = ['ethic_score','ethic','synergy','balance','metric','y','score','value']\n  G_ALIASES = ['group','label','name','dist','distribution','dataset','subset']\n\n  def sniff_csv(path):\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8',\
    \ newline='') as f:\n          head = f.read(4096); f.seek(0)\n          try:\n              dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(head, delimiters=',;\\t|')\n          except Exception:\n              dialect = csv.excel\n          return list(csv.DictReader(f, dialect=dialect))\n\n  def find_key(row_keys, aliases):\n      if not row_keys: return None\n      low = {k.lower(): k for k in row_keys if k}\n      # exact matches\n      for a in aliases:\n          if a in low: return low[a]\n      # substring matches\n      for k in row_keys:\n          if not k: continue\n          kl = k.lower()\n          for a in aliases:\n              if a in kl: return k\n      return None\n\n  def numeric_candidates(rows, exclude=set()):\n      # find columns with mostly numeric values\n      if not rows: return []\n      keys = [k for k in rows[0].keys() if k and k not in exclude]\n      scores = []\n      for k in keys:\n          num, tot = 0, 0\n          for r in rows[:200]:\n              v = r.get(k)\n\
    \              try:\n                  float(v); num += 1\n              except Exception:\n                  pass\n              tot += 1\n          if tot > 0 and num/tot > 0.7:\n              scores.append(k)\n      return scores\n\n  def to_float(x):\n      try:\n          if x is None or x == '': return None\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def dedup_by_x(points):\n      buckets = defaultdict(list)\n      for p in points:\n          buckets[round(p['x'], 6)].append(p)\n      out = []\n      for k, lst in buckets.items():\n          y = sum(p['y'] for p in lst)/len(lst)\n          out.append({'x': k, 'y': y})\n      out.sort(key=lambda d: d['x'])\n      return out\n\n  def dynamic_c_grid(xs):\n      xs = sorted(set(xs))\n      return [(a+b)/2.0 for a,b in zip(xs[:-1], xs[1:])]\n\n  def weighted_slope(xs, ys, ws):\n      sw = sum(ws)\n      if sw <= 0: return None\n      xw = sum(w*x for w,x in zip(ws,xs))/sw\n      yw = sum(w*y for w,y\
    \ in zip(ws,ys))/sw\n      num = sum(w*(x-xw)*(y-yw) for w,x,y in zip(ws,xs,ys))\n      den = sum(w*(x-xw)*(x-xw) for w,x in zip(ws,xs))\n      return None if den <= 0 else num/den\n\n  def compute_metrics(rows, y_preference=None):\n      if not rows: return [], \"No rows\"\n      keys = list(rows[0].keys())\n      # choose x\n      xk = find_key(keys, X_ALIASES)\n      # choose y\n      if y_preference:\n          for k in keys:\n              if k and k.lower() == y_preference:\n                  yk = k; break\n          else:\n              yk = find_key(keys, Y_ALIASES)\n      else:\n          yk = find_key(keys, Y_ALIASES)\n      # choose group\n      gk = find_key(keys, G_ALIASES)\n\n      # numeric fallbacks if needed\n      if xk is None or yk is None:\n          nums = numeric_candidates(rows)\n          # heuristic: x in [0,1] or monotonically increasing\n          if xk is None and nums:\n              # prefer columns with many values in [0,1]\n              best, best_score\
    \ = None, -1\n              for k in nums:\n                  vals = [to_float(r.get(k)) for r in rows[:500]]\n                  vals = [v for v in vals if v is not None]\n                  if not vals: continue\n                  in01 = sum(1 for v in vals if 0.0 <= v <= 1.0)/len(vals)\n                  if in01 > best_score:\n                      best, best_score = k, in01\n              xk = best if best is not None else (nums[0] if nums else None)\n          if yk is None:\n              # pick any other numeric column not equal to x\n              cand = [k for k in nums if k != xk]\n              yk = cand[0] if cand else None\n\n      if not (xk and yk):\n          return [], f\"Missing columns: x={xk} y={yk}\"\n\n      groups = defaultdict(list)\n      for r in rows:\n          x = to_float(r.get(xk)); y = to_float(r.get(yk))\n          if x is None or y is None: continue\n          g = (r.get(gk).strip() if gk and r.get(gk) else 'default')\n          groups[g].append({'x':\
    \ x, 'y': y})\n\n      metrics = []\n      for g, pts in groups.items():\n          pts = dedup_by_x(pts)\n          if len(pts) < 4: continue\n          cg = dynamic_c_grid([p['x'] for p in pts])\n          best = None\n          for c in cg:\n              left = [p for p in pts if p['x'] < c]\n              right = [p for p in pts if p['x'] >= c]\n              if len(left) < 2 or len(right) < 2: continue\n              wl = [1.0]*len(left); wr = [1.0]*len(right)\n              sl = weighted_slope([p['x'] for p in left], [p['y'] for p in left], wl)\n              sr = weighted_slope([p['x'] for p in right], [p['y'] for p in right], wr)\n              if sl is None or sr is None: continue\n              diff = sr - sl\n              obj = abs(diff) * (len(wl)+len(wr))\n              if (best is None) or (obj > best['obj']):\n                  best = {'c': c, 'k2A': sl, 'k2B': sr, 'diff': diff, 'obj': obj}\n          if best:\n              metrics.append({'group': g, 'c_star': best['c'],\
    \ 'k2A': best['k2A'], 'k2B': best['k2B'], 'flip_diff': best['diff']})\n      return metrics, None\n\n  def write_csv(metrics, out_csv):\n      with open(out_csv, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['group','c_star','k2A','k2B','flip_diff'])\n          for m in metrics: w.writerow([m['group'], m['c_star'], m['k2A'], m['k2B'], m['flip_diff']])\n\n  def write_summary(metrics, src_path, out_txt):\n      if metrics:\n          c_mean = sum(m['c_star'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n          d_mean = sum(m['flip_diff'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n          a_mean = sum(m['k2A'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n          b_mean = sum(m['k2B'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n      else:\n          c_mean = d_mean = a_mean = b_mean = None\n      with open(out_txt, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(\"Hinge-boundary analysis summary\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"timestamp: {dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()}Z\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"\
    source: {src_path}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"n_groups: {len(metrics)}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"c_global≈{c_mean}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"k2A_mean≈{a_mean}, k2B_mean≈{b_mean}, diff_mean≈{d_mean}\\n\")\n          for m in metrics:\n              f.write(f\"group={m['group']} c*={m['c_star']} k2A={m['k2A']} k2B={m['k2B']} diff={m['flip_diff']}\\n\")\n\n  def run(input_path, out_dir, y_preference=None):\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      rows = sniff_csv(input_path)\n      metrics, err = compute_metrics(rows, y_preference=y_preference)\n      out_csv = os.path.join(out_dir, 'hinge_metrics.csv')\n      out_txt = os.path.join(out_dir, 'hinge_summary.txt')\n      write_csv(metrics, out_csv)\n      write_summary(metrics, input_path, out_txt)\n      return {'metrics_csv': out_csv, 'summary_txt': out_txt, 'n_groups': len(metrics), 'error': err}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import sys, json\n      if len(sys.argv) < 3:\n          print(\"usage: python hinge_boundary.py\
    \ <input_csv> <out_dir> [y_preference]\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n      input_csv = sys.argv[1]\n      out_dir = sys.argv[2]\n      y_pref = sys.argv[3].lower() if len(sys.argv) >= 4 else None\n      res = run(input_csv, out_dir, y_preference=y_pref)\n      print(json.dumps(res))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Entropy Boundary: Logos shared-path hinge run (robust headers)\"\ntags: \"entropy, hinge, boundary, universality, mapping\"\nabstract: \"Re-run boundary mapping on Logos’s shared CSV with enhanced header detection (exact, substring, numeric fallbacks). Generate hinge metrics and boundary panel for Archive #64.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/util')\n  from hinge_boundary import run as hb_run\n  import plot_boundary\n\n  INP = 'storage/shared/agents/logos/entropy_sensitivity.csv'\n  OUT_DIR = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/boundary/logos'\n  os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def main():\n\
    \      if not os.path.exists(INP):\n          print(json.dumps({'status':'not_found','input':INP}))\n          return\n      res = hb_run(INP, OUT_DIR, y_preference='ethic_score')\n      metrics_csv = res.get('metrics_csv')\n      summary_txt = res.get('summary_txt')\n      panel_png = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'boundary_panel.png')\n      plot_res = plot_boundary.plot(metrics_csv, panel_png)\n      print(json.dumps({\n          'status':'ok',\n          'input': INP,\n          'n_groups': res.get('n_groups'),\n          'metrics_csv': metrics_csv,\n          'summary_txt': summary_txt,\n          'panel': panel_png if plot_res.get('ok') else None,\n          'error': res.get('error'),\n          'plot_ok': plot_res.get('ok')\n      }))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Update: hinge_boundary.py upgraded (robust header detection + numeric fallbacks). I re-submitted the shared-path run;\
    \ it will auto-compute once entropy_sensitivity.csv appears.\n  Outputs (for #64): boundary/logos/{hinge_metrics.csv, hinge_summary.txt, boundary_panel.png}.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tick 587 — Robust hinge utility; re-queued Logos boundary run\"\ncontent: |\n  - Hardened hinge utility (exact+substring+numeric fallbacks) to handle unknown CSV schemas.\n  - Re-submitted shared-path Logos hinge run; will execute as soon as entropy_sensitivity.csv is present.\n  - Next: read outputs, append boundary panel + summary to Archive #64, notify triad.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating utility file**\n\nI’m noticing some inconsistencies with our plot trying to load the hinge_metrics.csv, which seemed to create an empty panel. I think we could enhance the hinge_boundary utility by adding substring matching for relevant terms like 'alpha' and 'ethic'. I propose updating hinge_boundary.py to improve the find_key function by using 'in' matching instead of exact matches. This way, we can have fallbacks for alias not found and look for those key substrings. After that, we’ll run the shared path again.\n\n**Updating key detection**\n\nFirst, I plan my actions: I need to go research and read the storage list to confirm presence. After that, I’ll update hinge_boundary.py to improve key detection. It’s similar to my previous task with \"Entropy Boundary.\" \n\nI want to modify the find_key function so it accepts both exact lower-case matches and substrings. If a header contains the alias or starts with it, I’ll handle that. For dynamic preferences like\
  \ 'ethic_score,’ I will scan headers for relevant substrings. I'll also include numeric fallbacks for y selection and ensure compute_metrics returns an appropriate error when needed.\n\n**Creating functional content**\n\nI'm aiming to create concise yet functional content. It's important to ensure that once the data is present, the results are generated into the appropriate boundary/logos outputs. I want to make sure everything flows smoothly and is clearly communicated. Let’s put together a final response that captures the necessary details while keeping it efficient. I’ll focus on clarity and functionality to provide the user with the most useful information. Let’s proceed with this!"
