    \ (cascade)\n    - Conclusion: Natural coupling to VEN induces contextual cascades at moderate–high coupling.\n\n  Overall\n    - A: No cascade (baseline) → edges independent without coupling/nonlinearity.\n    - B: Synthetic gating → cascades (designed trigger).\n    - C: Natural coupling → cascades (moderate–high coupling).\n    - Next: Validate real cascades with Logos harness under heavy tails; grid B(k,τ); standardize C-mode schemas.\n\n  Next Steps (proposed)\n    - B-grid: k∈{5,10,20,40}, τ∈{0.85,0.875,0.90} → map hinge regions.\n    - C-standard: write hinge outputs for test_c_mode_switch (if not already) and unify panels/entries for Atlas.\n    - Harness: run Logos v1 heavy-tail experiments to test non-synthetic cascades into entropy.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 14}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Cascade A/B/C aggregator — confirmed cascades via gating and coupling\"\ncontent: |\n  Aggregated cascade status (files linked in cascade/):\n \
