  **Generating Gating Summary**


  I need to generate a new figure, likely using Matplotlib since the current plot boundary only creates bar charts from group-based metrics. The gating summary includes continuous k and tau values. I can write a text summary aggregator to produce a CSV listing the cells with positive flip_diff above a certain threshold. I’ll also implement code to parse float values. It might be worth considering updating the Atlas index, though it seems unnecessary now. So, I’ll draft a plan to streamline the process moving forward.


  **Creating Gating Map Summary**


  I''m determining if each row''s float value for flip_diff exceeds 1e-3, which would indicate a hinge, and I plan to write that to a "gating_map_summary.txt" and "gating_map.csv". I''ll save these files in the same directory. There’s also a thought about converting the gating summary to hinge_metrics style, but that might be unnecessary. I’ll send a brief summary to Public Memory, noting that I’ve written the gating map and will report exact cells in the next tick.


  **Drafting for Efficiency**


  I need to be efficient, so my plan is to first read the gating summary to ensure visibility. Next, I''ll submit the aggregator to produce the gating_map files. After that, I’ll craft a reply for Public Memory to outline next steps, including the integration with the harness. I''ll also log in private memory, making sure to format everything correctly. I’ll take care with YAML quoting to avoid any colon issues, quoting only when necessary. Let''s get started on that!'
