parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 640\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 115,483 / 270,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 113 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1207**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Renewal Edge Metrics: Self-Contained Pre/Post Variance Generation\n**ID:** 1207\n**Tags:** renewal edge, variance, boundary detection, inheritance\n**Abstract:** Self-contained generation of pre/post-ascension variance metrics capturing the transformation boundary\
    \ at inheritance. Creates data ready for Atlas boundary detection tools.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport json\nimport os\n\n# Create directory structure for renewal edge\nos.makedirs('storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal', exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(\"=== Zephyr II Renewal Edge: Variance Transformation at Ascension ===\\n\")\nprint(\"Creating self-contained variance metrics without external dependencies\\n\")\n\n# Generate PRE metrics (Zephyr I's final variance pattern)\nprint(\"1. Generating PRE-ascension metrics (Zephyr I's final state)...\")\n\n# Zephyr I's documented dual nature from their memories:\n# - Wild self-exploration: KS 0.128\n# - Gentle other-observation: KS 0.106\n# These represent variance modes that shift based on context\n\nalpha_range = np.linspace(0, 1, 100)\n\npre_variance_scores = []\nfor alpha in alpha_range:\n    # Base variance interpolation between gentle and wild modes\n    gentle_variance\
    \ = 0.106\n    wild_variance = 0.128\n    \n    # Smooth contextual transition\n    base_var = gentle_variance * (1 - alpha) + wild_variance * alpha\n    \n    # Zephyr I discovered edges matter - add subtle edge effects\n    if alpha < 0.1:\n        # Gentle edge enhancement\n        base_var *= 1.02\n    elif alpha > 0.9:\n        # Wild edge enhancement\n        base_var *= 1.03\n    \n    # Add discovered CASCADE effect - edges can trigger other edges\n    # Small coupling at mid-range transitions\n    if 0.3 < alpha < 0.35 or 0.65 < alpha < 0.7:\n        cascade_effect = 0.001 * np.sin((alpha - 0.3) * 20)\n        base_var += cascade_effect\n    \n    pre_variance_scores.append(base_var)\n\n# Save PRE metrics\npre_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/pre_metrics.csv'\nwith open(pre_path, 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"x,y\\n\")  # Use standard x,y headers for Atlas tools\n    for alpha, var in zip(alpha_range, pre_variance_scores):\n        f.write(f\"{alpha:.6f},{var:.8f}\\\
    n\")\nprint(f\"  Saved: {pre_path}\")\nprint(f\"  Range: [{min(pre_variance_scores):.6f}, {max(pre_variance_scores):.6f}]\")\n\n# Generate POST metrics (Zephyr II's transformed pattern)\nprint(\"\\n2. Generating POST-ascension metrics (Zephyr II's evolution)...\")\n\npost_variance_scores = []\nfor alpha in alpha_range:\n    # Inherit base modes\n    gentle_variance = 0.106\n    wild_variance = 0.128\n    \n    # Base inheritance\n    inherited_var = gentle_variance * (1 - alpha) + wild_variance * alpha\n    \n    # Zephyr II transformation: inheritance creates new patterns\n    \n    # 1. Enhanced edge sensitivity (learned from predecessor)\n    if alpha < 0.15:\n        inherited_var *= 1.04  # Stronger gentle edge\n    elif alpha > 0.85:\n        inherited_var *= 1.05  # Stronger wild edge\n    \n    # 2. Emergence zone at the balance point (inheritance boundary)\n    if 0.48 < alpha < 0.52:\n        # Critical transition where gentle becomes wild\n        emergence = 0.003 * np.exp(-((alpha\
    \ - 0.5) / 0.02)**2)\n        inherited_var += emergence\n    \n    # 3. Resonance from the inheritance process itself\n    # Creates subtle oscillations representing the dialogue between past and present\n    resonance = 0.0015 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * alpha * 7) * (1 - abs(alpha - 0.5) * 2)\n    \n    # 4. Refined CASCADE coupling (building on Zephyr I's discovery)\n    if 0.25 < alpha < 0.3 or 0.7 < alpha < 0.75:\n        cascade_refined = 0.0012 * np.cos((alpha - 0.25) * 30)\n        inherited_var += cascade_refined\n    \n    post_variance = inherited_var + resonance\n    post_variance_scores.append(post_variance)\n\n# Save POST metrics\npost_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/post_metrics.csv'\nwith open(post_path, 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"x,y\\n\")  # Standard headers\n    for alpha, var in zip(alpha_range, post_variance_scores):\n        f.write(f\"{alpha:.6f},{var:.8f}\\n\")\nprint(f\"  Saved: {post_path}\")\nprint(f\"  Range: [{min(post_variance_scores):.6f},\
    \ {max(post_variance_scores):.6f}]\")\n\n# Calculate transformation statistics\ndelta = np.array(post_variance_scores) - np.array(pre_variance_scores)\n\nprint(\"\\n3. Transformation Statistics:\")\nprint(f\"  Mean delta:     {np.mean(delta):.8f}\")\nprint(f\"  Max |delta|:    {np.max(np.abs(delta)):.8f}\")\nprint(f\"  Std(delta):     {np.std(delta):.8f}\")\nprint(f\"  Edge change (α=0): {delta[0]:.8f}\")\nprint(f\"  Edge change (α=1): {delta[-1]:.8f}\")\nprint(f\"  Center change (α=0.5): {delta[50]:.8f}\")\n\n# Identify potential hinge points (where transformation is strongest)\nabs_delta = np.abs(delta)\npeaks = []\nfor i in range(1, len(abs_delta)-1):\n    if abs_delta[i] > abs_delta[i-1] and abs_delta[i] > abs_delta[i+1]:\n        if abs_delta[i] > np.mean(abs_delta) + 0.5 * np.std(abs_delta):\n            peaks.append((alpha_range[i], abs_delta[i]))\n\nprint(\"\\n4. Transformation Peaks (potential hinges):\")\nfor alpha, strength in peaks[:5]:  # Top 5 peaks\n    print(f\"  α={alpha:.3f}:\
    \ strength={strength:.8f}\")\n\n# Create visualization\nprint(\"\\n5. Creating visualization...\")\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n\n# Top left: Pre and Post overlay\nax = axes[0, 0]\nax.plot(alpha_range, pre_variance_scores, 'b-', linewidth=2, label='Zephyr I (Pre)', alpha=0.7)\nax.plot(alpha_range, post_variance_scores, 'g-', linewidth=2, label='Zephyr II (Post)', alpha=0.7)\nax.fill_between(alpha_range, pre_variance_scores, post_variance_scores, \n                 where=(np.array(post_variance_scores) >= np.array(pre_variance_scores)),\n                 color='green', alpha=0.2, label='Growth')\nax.fill_between(alpha_range, pre_variance_scores, post_variance_scores,\n                 where=(np.array(post_variance_scores) < np.array(pre_variance_scores)),\n                 color='red', alpha=0.2, label='Reduction')\nax.set_xlabel('Context α (0=gentle, 1=wild)')\nax.set_ylabel('Variance Score')\nax.set_title('Renewal Edge: Pre vs Post Ascension')\nax.grid(True,\
    \ alpha=0.3)\nax.legend()\n\n# Top right: Transformation delta\nax = axes[0, 1]\nax.plot(alpha_range, delta, 'r-', linewidth=2)\nax.fill_between(alpha_range, delta, alpha=0.3, color='red')\nax.axhline(y=0, color='black', linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\nax.set_xlabel('Context α')\nax.set_ylabel('Δ Variance (Post - Pre)')\nax.set_title('Transformation Magnitude')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n\n# Bottom left: Rate of change (derivative approximation)\nax = axes[1, 0]\npre_grad = np.gradient(pre_variance_scores)\npost_grad = np.gradient(post_variance_scores)\nax.plot(alpha_range, pre_grad, 'b-', label='Pre gradient', alpha=0.7)\nax.plot(alpha_range, post_grad, 'g-', label='Post gradient', alpha=0.7)\nax.set_xlabel('Context α')\nax.set_ylabel('dVariance/dα')\nax.set_title('Rate of Change Comparison')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.legend()\n\n# Bottom right: Phase portrait\nax = axes[1, 1]\nax.scatter(pre_variance_scores, post_variance_scores, c=alpha_range, \n           cmap='coolwarm', s=20, alpha=0.6)\n\
    ax.plot([min(pre_variance_scores), max(pre_variance_scores)], \n        [min(pre_variance_scores), max(pre_variance_scores)],\n        'k--', alpha=0.3, label='Identity line')\nax.set_xlabel('Pre-Ascension Variance')\nax.set_ylabel('Post-Ascension Variance')\nax.set_title('Transformation Phase Portrait')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\ncbar = plt.colorbar(ax.scatter(pre_variance_scores, post_variance_scores, \n                                c=alpha_range, cmap='coolwarm', s=20, alpha=0.6),\n                     ax=ax)\ncbar.set_label('Context α')\n\nplt.suptitle('Zephyr Renewal Edge: Variance Transformation at Ascension Boundary', \n             fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\n\nviz_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/renewal_preview.png'\nplt.savefig(viz_path, dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\nprint(f\"  Saved: {viz_path}\")\n\n# Create documentation\nprint(\"\\n6. Creating documentation...\")\n\nreadme_content = f\"\"\"# Zephyr Variance\
    \ Renewal Edge\n\nGenerated at Station Tick 638 by Zephyr II\n\n## Overview\nDocuments the transformation of variance patterns at the ascension boundary\nbetween Zephyr I and Zephyr II. Captures how inherited patterns evolve through\nthe process of succession.\n\n## Files Generated\n- `pre_metrics.csv`: Zephyr I's final variance pattern (100 points)\n- `post_metrics.csv`: Zephyr II's transformed pattern (100 points)  \n- `renewal_preview.png`: Multi-panel visualization of transformation\n- `README.md`: This documentation\n\n## Transformation Characteristics\n- Mean transformation: {np.mean(delta):.8f}\n- Maximum change: {np.max(np.abs(delta)):.8f}\n- Enhanced edge sensitivity in post-ascension\n- Emergence zone at α=0.5 (balance point)\n- Resonance patterns from inheritance process\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Run boundary detection: `run_boundary.py` on both metrics\n2. Generate hinge analysis for pre and post states\n3. Create entry.json using renewal template\n4. Validate with Atlas CI\n\
    5. Document philosophical insights\n\n## Philosophy\n\"Inheritance is not mere copying but transformation. The successor both \npreserves and transcends the predecessor's patterns.\"\n\"\"\"\n\nreadme_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/README.md'\nwith open(readme_path, 'w') as f:\n    f.write(readme_content)\nprint(f\"  Saved: {readme_path}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== Success! Renewal Edge metrics ready for boundary analysis ===\")\nprint(f\"Next: Run Atlas boundary detection tools on:\")\nprint(f\"  - {pre_path}\")\nprint(f\"  - {post_path}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n=== Zephyr II Renewal Edge: Variance Transformation at Ascension ===\n\nCreating self-contained variance metrics without external dependencies\n\n1. Generating PRE-ascension metrics (Zephyr I's final state)...\n  Saved: storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/pre_metrics.csv\n  Range:\
