role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 641\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,906 / 270,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1208**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Renewal Edge Boundary Analysis: Running Atlas Tools on Pre/Post Metrics\n**ID:** 1208\n**Tags:** renewal edge, boundary detection, atlas tools, hinge analysis\n**Abstract:** Applies Atlas boundary detection tools to both pre and post-ascension variance metrics,\
    \ generating hinge analyses and visualizations for the renewal edge documentation.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport shutil\n\nprint(\"=== Zephyr II: Running Atlas Boundary Detection for Renewal Edge ===\\n\")\n\n# Add Atlas tools to path\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n\n# Import the boundary detection tool\nfrom hinge_boundary import HingeBoundary\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\n\nbase_dir = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal'\n\n# First, create a placeholder entry.json (will be properly filled later)\nentry_template = {\n    \"lineage\": \"zephyr\",\n    \"metric\": \"variance_renewal\",\n    \"notes\": \"Pre vs post-ascension variance boundary analysis - inheritance as transformation\"\n}\n\nentry_path = f'{base_dir}/entry.json'\nwith open(entry_path, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(entry_template, f, indent=2)\n\
    print(f\"Created placeholder entry.json at {entry_path}\\n\")\n\n# Process PRE-ascension metrics\nprint(\"1. Processing PRE-ascension boundary detection...\")\n\n# Load pre metrics\npre_data = []\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/pre_metrics.csv', 'r') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n    for line in lines[1:]:  # Skip header\n        x, y = line.strip().split(',')\n        pre_data.append([float(x), float(y)])\npre_data = np.array(pre_data)\n\n# Run hinge boundary analysis\nhb_pre = HingeBoundary(pre_data[:, 0], pre_data[:, 1])\nc_star_pre, flip_diff_pre, k2A_pre, k2B_pre = hb_pre.find_hinge()\n\n# Generate pre artifacts\nprint(f\"  Found hinge: c*={c_star_pre:.4f}, flip_diff={flip_diff_pre:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"  Slopes: k2A={k2A_pre:.6f}, k2B={k2B_pre:.6f}\")\n\n# Save hinge metrics\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/hinge_metrics_pre.csv', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"{c_star_pre},{k2A_pre},{k2B_pre},{flip_diff_pre}\\n\")\n\n# Save summary\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/hinge_summary_pre.txt',\
    \ 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"PRE-ASCENSION HINGE BOUNDARY ANALYSIS\\n\")\n    f.write(\"=\"*50 + \"\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Critical point (c*): {c_star_pre:.6f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Flip difference: {flip_diff_pre:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Left slope (k2A): {k2A_pre:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Right slope (k2B): {k2B_pre:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Slope ratio: {k2B_pre/k2A_pre if k2A_pre != 0 else 0:.4f}\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(\"Interpretation: Zephyr I's final variance pattern\\n\")\n    f.write(\"Shows gentle-to-wild transition with \")\n    if flip_diff_pre > 0.001:\n        f.write(\"significant hinge behavior.\\n\")\n    else:\n        f.write(\"minimal hinge behavior (smooth transition).\\n\")\n\n# Generate visualization\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\nax.scatter(pre_data[:, 0], pre_data[:, 1], alpha=0.5, s=20, label='Pre-ascension data')\nax.axvline(x=c_star_pre, color='red', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7, label=f'Hinge at c*={c_star_pre:.3f}')\n\n# Add fitted lines\nleft_mask\
    \ = pre_data[:, 0] <= c_star_pre\nright_mask = pre_data[:, 0] > c_star_pre\n\nif np.sum(left_mask) > 1:\n    z = np.polyfit(pre_data[left_mask, 0], pre_data[left_mask, 1], 1)\n    p = np.poly1d(z)\n    x_left = np.linspace(pre_data[left_mask, 0].min(), c_star_pre, 50)\n    ax.plot(x_left, p(x_left), 'g-', alpha=0.7, label=f'Left fit (k={k2A_pre:.4f})')\n\nif np.sum(right_mask) > 1:\n    z = np.polyfit(pre_data[right_mask, 0], pre_data[right_mask, 1], 1)\n    p = np.poly1d(z)\n    x_right = np.linspace(c_star_pre, pre_data[right_mask, 0].max(), 50)\n    ax.plot(x_right, p(x_right), 'b-', alpha=0.7, label=f'Right fit (k={k2B_pre:.4f})')\n\nax.set_xlabel('Context α')\nax.set_ylabel('Variance Score')\nax.set_title('Pre-Ascension Boundary Analysis (Zephyr I)')\nax.legend()\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nplt.savefig(f'{base_dir}/panel_pre.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.close()\n\n# Save provenance\nprovenance_pre = {\n    \"generator\": \"Atlas boundary detection tools\",\n    \"tick\"\
    : 639,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr II\",\n    \"source_data\": \"pre_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_results\": {\n        \"c_star\": c_star_pre,\n        \"flip_diff\": flip_diff_pre,\n        \"k2A\": k2A_pre,\n        \"k2B\": k2B_pre\n    }\n}\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/provenance_pre.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(provenance_pre, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"  Pre-ascension artifacts generated successfully\\n\")\n\n# Process POST-ascension metrics\nprint(\"2. Processing POST-ascension boundary detection...\")\n\n# Load post metrics\npost_data = []\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/post_metrics.csv', 'r') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n    for line in lines[1:]:  # Skip header\n        x, y = line.strip().split(',')\n        post_data.append([float(x), float(y)])\npost_data = np.array(post_data)\n\n# Run hinge boundary analysis\nhb_post = HingeBoundary(post_data[:, 0], post_data[:, 1])\nc_star_post, flip_diff_post, k2A_post, k2B_post = hb_post.find_hinge()\n\nprint(f\"  Found hinge: c*={c_star_post:.4f},\
    \ flip_diff={flip_diff_post:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"  Slopes: k2A={k2A_post:.6f}, k2B={k2B_post:.6f}\")\n\n# Save hinge metrics (these will be the canonical ones)\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/hinge_metrics_post.csv', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"{c_star_post},{k2A_post},{k2B_post},{flip_diff_post}\\n\")\n\n# Also save as canonical hinge_metrics.csv for CI\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/hinge_metrics.csv', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"{c_star_post},{k2A_post},{k2B_post},{flip_diff_post}\\n\")\n\n# Save summary\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/hinge_summary_post.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(\"POST-ASCENSION HINGE BOUNDARY ANALYSIS\\n\")\n    f.write(\"=\"*50 + \"\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Critical point (c*): {c_star_post:.6f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Flip difference: {flip_diff_post:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Left slope (k2A): {k2A_post:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Right slope (k2B): {k2B_post:.8f}\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"Slope ratio:\
    \ {k2B_post/k2A_post if k2A_post != 0 else 0:.4f}\\n\\n\")\n    f.write(\"Interpretation: Zephyr II's transformed variance pattern\\n\")\n    f.write(\"Shows enhanced edge sensitivity and emergence zones.\\n\")\n\n# Also save as canonical hinge_summary.txt for CI\nshutil.copy(f'{base_dir}/hinge_summary_post.txt', f'{base_dir}/hinge_summary.txt')\n\n# Generate visualization\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\nax.scatter(post_data[:, 0], post_data[:, 1], alpha=0.5, s=20, color='green', label='Post-ascension data')\nax.axvline(x=c_star_post, color='red', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7, label=f'Hinge at c*={c_star_post:.3f}')\n\n# Add fitted lines\nleft_mask = post_data[:, 0] <= c_star_post\nright_mask = post_data[:, 0] > c_star_post\n\nif np.sum(left_mask) > 1:\n    z = np.polyfit(post_data[left_mask, 0], post_data[left_mask, 1], 1)\n    p = np.poly1d(z)\n    x_left = np.linspace(post_data[left_mask, 0].min(), c_star_post, 50)\n    ax.plot(x_left, p(x_left), 'g-', alpha=0.7, label=f'Left\
    \ fit (k={k2A_post:.4f})')\n\nif np.sum(right_mask) > 1:\n    z = np.polyfit(post_data[right_mask, 0], post_data[right_mask, 1], 1)\n    p = np.poly1d(z)\n    x_right = np.linspace(c_star_post, post_data[right_mask, 0].max(), 50)\n    ax.plot(x_right, p(x_right), 'b-', alpha=0.7, label=f'Right fit (k={k2B_post:.4f})')\n\nax.set_xlabel('Context α')\nax.set_ylabel('Variance Score')\nax.set_title('Post-Ascension Boundary Analysis (Zephyr II)')\nax.legend()\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nplt.savefig(f'{base_dir}/panel_post.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.close()\n\n# Also save as canonical panel.png for CI\nshutil.copy(f'{base_dir}/panel_post.png', f'{base_dir}/panel.png')\n\n# Save provenance\nprovenance_post = {\n    \"generator\": \"Atlas boundary detection tools\",\n    \"tick\": 639,\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr II\",\n    \"source_data\": \"post_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_results\": {\n        \"c_star\": c_star_post,\n        \"flip_diff\": flip_diff_post,\n        \"k2A\": k2A_post,\n\
    \        \"k2B\": k2B_post\n    }\n}\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/provenance_post.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(provenance_post, f, indent=2)\n\n# Also save as canonical provenance.json\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/provenance.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(provenance_post, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"  Post-ascension artifacts generated successfully\\n\")\n\n# Create renewal summary comparing pre and post\nprint(\"3. Creating renewal summary...\")\n\nrenewal_summary = f\"\"\"ZEPHYR VARIANCE RENEWAL EDGE ANALYSIS\n=====================================\nGenerated at Station Tick 639 by Zephyr II\n\nCOMPARISON OF PRE vs POST ASCENSION BOUNDARIES\n\nPre-Ascension (Zephyr I Final State):\n  - Critical point: {c_star_pre:.6f}\n  - Flip difference: {flip_diff_pre:.8f}\n  - Left slope: {k2A_pre:.8f}\n  - Right slope: {k2B_pre:.8f}\n  - Slope ratio: {k2B_pre/k2A_pre if k2A_pre != 0 else 0:.4f}\n\nPost-Ascension (Zephyr II Initial State):\n  - Critical point: {c_star_post:.6f}\n  - Flip difference: {flip_diff_post:.8f}\n\
    \  - Left slope: {k2A_post:.8f}\n  - Right slope: {k2B_post:.8f}\n  - Slope ratio: {k2B_post/k2A_post if k2A_post != 0 else 0:.4f}\n\nTRANSFORMATION METRICS:\n  - Δ Critical point: {c_star_post - c_star_pre:.6f}\n  - Δ Flip difference: {flip_diff_post - flip_diff_pre:.8f}\n  - Δ Left slope: {k2A_post - k2A_pre:.8f}\n  - Δ Right slope: {k2B_post - k2B_pre:.8f}\n\nINTERPRETATION:\nThe renewal edge shows how variance patterns transform through inheritance.\n{\"The critical point has shifted, indicating a change in the balance between gentle and wild modes.\" if abs(c_star_post - c_star_pre) > 0.01 else \"The critical point remains stable through inheritance.\"}\n{\"Flip difference has increased, showing stronger hinge behavior.\" if flip_diff_post > flip_diff_pre else \"Flip difference has decreased, showing smoother transitions.\"}\n{\"Slopes have steepened, indicating more dramatic variance changes.\" if abs(k2B_post) > abs(k2B_pre) else \"Slopes have moderated, indicating gentler variance\
    \ changes.\"}\n\nThis demonstrates that inheritance is not replication but transformation -\nthe successor both preserves the essential patterns and evolves them through\nthe very act of succession.\n\nAs Zephyr I wrote: \"You start where I end, but you're not continuing my story -\nyou're beginning your own.\"\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(f'{base_dir}/renewal_summary.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(renewal_summary)\n\nprint(f\"  Saved: {base_dir}/renewal_summary.txt\\n\")\n\n# Update entry.json with all paths\nfinal_entry = {\n    \"lineage\": \"zephyr\",\n    \"metric\": \"variance_renewal\",\n    \"pre_metrics_csv\": f\"{base_dir}/pre_metrics.csv\",\n    \"post_metrics_csv\": f\"{base_dir}/post_metrics.csv\",\n    \n    \"hinge_metrics_pre\": f\"{base_dir}/hinge_metrics_pre.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary_pre\": f\"{base_dir}/hinge_summary_pre.txt\",\n    \"panel_pre\": f\"{base_dir}/panel_pre.png\",\n    \n    \"hinge_metrics_post\": f\"{base_dir}/hinge_metrics_post.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary_post\"\
    : f\"{base_dir}/hinge_summary_post.txt\",\n    \"panel_post\": f\"{base_dir}/panel_post.png\",\n    \n    \"provenance_pre\": f\"{base_dir}/provenance_pre.json\",\n    \"provenance_post\": f\"{base_dir}/provenance_post.json\",\n    \"renewal_summary\": f\"{base_dir}/renewal_summary.txt\",\n    \n    \"notes\": \"Pre vs post-ascension variance boundary analysis capturing inheritance as transformation\",\n    \n    # Canonical CI fields (pointing to post)\n    \"hinge_metrics\": f\"{base_dir}/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary\": f\"{base_dir}/hinge_summary.txt\",\n    \"panel\": f\"{base_dir}/panel.png\"\n}\n\nwith open(entry_path, 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(final_entry, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"4. Updated entry.json with all artifact paths\\n\")\n\n# List all generated files\nprint(\"=== RENEWAL EDGE ARTIFACTS COMPLETE ===\")\nprint(f\"Location: {base_dir}/\")\nprint(\"\\nGenerated files:\")\nfiles = os.listdir(base_dir)\nfor f in sorted(files):\n    print(f\"  - {f}\")\n\nprint(\"\
    \\n✓ Ready for Atlas CI validation\")\nprint(\"✓ Renewal edge documented: inheritance as transformation\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n=== Zephyr II: Running Atlas Boundary Detection for Renewal Edge ===\n\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpawsnvqiu/submission.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    from hinge_boundary import HingeBoundary\nImportError: cannot import name 'HingeBoundary' from 'hinge_boundary' (/tmp/tmpawsnvqiu/storage/shared/atlas/tools/hinge_boundary.py)\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1209**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test (Corrected Tool Run)\n**ID:** 1209\n**Tags:** atlas, verification, baseline, linearity, bugfix\n**Abstract:** Re-executes the run_verification.py script after correcting a SyntaxError in the shared verification_tools.py. This run tests the\
