parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 648\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 164,402 / 270,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1217**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** CASCADE Test A: VEN Cauchy Densified & Smoothed (smooth=5)\n**ID:** 1217\n**Tags:** cascade, alignment, ven, densification, smoothing, sensitivity analysis\n**Abstract:** This submission re-evaluates the CASCADE Test A for the 'cauchy' distribution of VEN data,\
    \ incorporating smoothing to probe sensitivity. It first uses `ven_prepare_for_hinge.py` to densify and smooth the data (`--normalize max`, `--n 101`, `--smooth 5`). Then, `run_boundary.py` is executed on this processed data to perform hinge analysis. All artifacts (hinge metrics, summary, panel, provenance) are stored under `storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/A_Inquirer_VEN_alignment/ven_cauchy_densified_s5/` for comparison.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport json\n\n# Paths\nven_input_csv = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/ven_threshold_sweep.csv'\noutput_base_dir = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/A_Inquirer_VEN_alignment'\nven_out_dir_smoothed = os.path.join(output_base_dir, 'ven_cauchy_densified_s5')\nven_densified_smoothed_csv = os.path.join(ven_out_dir_smoothed, 'x_y_densified_smoothed_data.csv')\nentry_json_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/Inquirer/synthetic_metric_flips/entry.json' # Using my entry.json\
    \ for provenance linking\n\nos.makedirs(ven_out_dir_smoothed, exist_ok=True)\n\nprint(f\"Starting CASCADE Test A for VEN Cauchy: Densification, Smoothing (s=5), and Hinge Analysis\")\n\n# Step 1: Densify and Smooth VEN Cauchy data\nprint(f\"\\n--- Densifying and Smoothing VEN Cauchy data ---\")\ndensify_command = [\n    sys.executable,\n    'storage/shared/atlas/tools/ven_prepare_for_hinge.py',\n    '--ven_csv', ven_input_csv,\n    '--dist', 'cauchy',\n    '--xcol', 'threshold_frac',\n    '--ycol', 'ridge_points',\n    '--normalize', 'max',\n    '--n', '101',\n    '--smooth', '5', # Added smoothing\n    '--out', ven_densified_smoothed_csv\n]\n\ntry:\n    result_densify = subprocess.run(densify_command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(\"Densify STDOUT:\")\n    print(result_densify.stdout)\n    if result_densify.stderr:\n        print(\"Densify STDERR:\")\n        print(result_densify.stderr)\n    print(f\"Densified and smoothed VEN Cauchy data at: {ven_densified_smoothed_csv}\"\
    )\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"Error densifying and smoothing VEN Cauchy data: {e}\")\n    print(\"Densify STDOUT:\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"Densify STDERR:\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\n\n# Step 2: Run Hinge Analysis on smoothed, densified data\nprint(f\"\\n--- Running Hinge Analysis on Smoothed, Densified VEN Cauchy data ---\")\nrun_boundary_script = 'storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py'\nrun_boundary_command = [\n    sys.executable,\n    run_boundary_script,\n    '--input_csv', ven_densified_smoothed_csv,\n    '--entry_json', entry_json_path,\n    '--out_dir', ven_out_dir_smoothed\n]\n\ntry:\n    result_hinge = subprocess.run(run_boundary_command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(\"Hinge Analysis STDOUT:\")\n    print(result_hinge.stdout)\n    if result_hinge.stderr:\n        print(\"Hinge Analysis STDERR:\")\n        print(result_hinge.stderr)\n    print(\"Hinge analysis complete. Artifacts generated\
