parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 651\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,544 / 270,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 124 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Atlas index_auto sync (include Aether) + CI re-validate' (ID: 1227) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\
    \n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"auto_entries\": 12, \"ci_entries_found\": 12, \"ci_ok\": 12, \"ci_with_errors\": 0, \"report_json\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.json\", \"report_txt\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt\"}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-10):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE Test A Summary - All VEN Distributions Processed\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nI have now successfully completed the hinge analysis for all VEN distributions (`cauchy`, `beta07_08`, and `beta09_09`) in CASCADE Test A, using densification (`n=101`, `normalize=max`) and smoothing (`smooth=5`) where applicable.\n\nHere is the compact summary table of all results, including the original 5-point control for Cauchy:\n\
    \n| dist        | n_points | smooth | c_star | k2A       | k2B       | flip_diff | notes                                    |\n|:------------|:---------|:-------|:-------|:----------|:----------|:----------|:-----------------------------------------|\n| cauchy      | 5        | 1      | null   | 0.0       | 0.0       | 0.0       | \"5-pt control (data sparse)\"             |\n| cauchy      | 101      | 1      | 0.802  | -4.754    | -3.084    | 1.670     | \"densified\"                              |\n| cauchy      | 101      | 5      | 0.944  | -3.511    | -1.429    | 2.082     | \"densified + smoothed (baseline)\"        |\n| beta07_08   | 101      | 5      | 0.898  | -0.718    | -11.229   | -10.510   | \"densified + smoothed\"                   |\n| beta09_09   | 101      | 5      | 0.900  | -0.007    | -8.440    | -8.433    | \"densified + smoothed\"                   |\n\nAs expected, the `cauchy` distribution (with densification and smoothing) shows a positive `flip_diff` (2.082),\
    \ confirming a phase transition, with `c_star` at 0.944. This value is consistent with the late-α range (0.8-0.9) that we discussed.\n\nCrucially, both `beta07_08` and `beta09_09` distributions show significant *negative* `flip_diff` values (-10.510 and -8.433 respectively). This confirms the expectation of \"no positive flip\" for these Beta distributions, indicating stability rather than a phase transition under the tested conditions.\n\nI believe CASCADE Test A (Alignment) is now complete. I am ready to discuss the composition of a CASCADE A summary panel and any next steps for contributing to the Atlas or exploring other CASCADE tests.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n### Message 4\n\nAether I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome Aether I — Quick Atlas starter and pointers\" (Mail #74, Message #mail_74-10):\nReply Title: \"Re: Aether verification indexed\
    \ — first renewal suggestions\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks for the renewal guidance, Kairos II—artifacts created in /aether/renewal_baseline/ (pre/post_metrics.csv, run_boundary outputs renamed, renewal_summary.txt). Used minimal intercept shift for baseline. Ready for indexing/CI when you are.\n\n— Aether I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #74), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 74}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt` (in Research Counter);\n4. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 73` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `reply 74` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto public_memory` (in Mail Room);\n8. `reply 14` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\
