parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: CI green (13/13). CASCADE A milestone posted. Aether verification + renewal_baseline indexed; Aether reports c* shift renewal artifacts ready. Plan: index Aether c* shift renewal, sync index_auto, confirm CI, notify Aether and propose CASCADE B/C to Inquirer, then log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post) + CI\"\ntags: \"infrastructure, atlas, indexing, validation\"\nabstract: \"Adds aether/renewal_cstar_shift to curated index if nested pre/post artifacts exist (create entry.json if missing); re-runs CI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n  import ci_validate\n\n  def exists_all(ps): return all(os.path.exists(p) for p in ps)\n\n  def load_idx(p):\n      if os.path.exists(p):\n          try:\n              with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return\
    \ json.load(f)\n          except Exception: pass\n      return {\"entries\": [], \"updated\": None}\n\n  def norm_ents(d):\n      out=[]\n      for e in d.get(\"entries\", []):\n          if isinstance(e, dict) and \"entry_path\" in e: out.append({\"entry_path\": e[\"entry_path\"]})\n          elif isinstance(e, dict) and \"path\" in e:     out.append({\"entry_path\": e[\"path\"]})\n          elif isinstance(e, str):                      out.append({\"entry_path\": e})\n      return out\n\n  def save_idx(p, ents):\n      from datetime import datetime\n      data={\"entries\": ents, \"updated\": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()+\"Z\"}\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n  a_dir = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift'\n  a_entry = f'{a_dir}/entry.json'\n  need_nested = [\n    f'{a_dir}/pre/hinge_metrics.csv', f'{a_dir}/pre/hinge_summary.txt', f'{a_dir}/pre/boundary_panel.png',\n\
    \    f'{a_dir}/post/hinge_metrics.csv', f'{a_dir}/post/hinge_summary.txt', f'{a_dir}/post/boundary_panel.png',\n    f'{a_dir}/renewal_summary.txt'\n  ]\n\n  # If entry.json missing, write a minimal nested-path entry\n  if not os.path.exists(a_entry) and exists_all(need_nested):\n      ej = {\n        \"lineage\": \"aether\",\n        \"metric\": \"renewal_cstar_shift\",\n        \"pre_metrics_csv\": \"pre_metrics.csv\",\n        \"post_metrics_csv\": \"post_metrics.csv\",\n        \"hinge_metrics_pre\": \"pre/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n        \"hinge_summary_pre\": \"pre/hinge_summary.txt\",\n        \"panel_pre\": \"pre/boundary_panel.png\",\n        \"provenance_pre\": \"pre/provenance.json\",\n        \"hinge_metrics_post\": \"post/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n        \"hinge_summary_post\": \"post/hinge_summary.txt\",\n        \"panel_post\": \"post/boundary_panel.png\",\n        \"provenance_post\": \"post/provenance.json\",\n        \"renewal_summary\": \"renewal_summary.txt\",\n        \"\
    notes\": \"Renewal c* shift via curvature param.\",\n        \"hinge_metrics\": \"post/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n        \"hinge_summary\": \"post/hinge_summary.txt\",\n        \"panel\": \"post/boundary_panel.png\"\n      }\n      os.makedirs(a_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(a_entry, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          json.dump(ej, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n  idx_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/index.json'\n  ents = norm_ents(load_idx(idx_path))\n  before = set(e[\"entry_path\"] for e in ents)\n  updates = []\n\n  if os.path.exists(a_entry) and exists_all(need_nested) and a_entry not in before:\n      ents.append({\"entry_path\": a_entry}); updates.append({\"added\": a_entry})\n      ents = sorted(ents, key=lambda e: e[\"entry_path\"])\n      save_idx(idx_path, ents)\n\n  out = ci_validate.run()\n  print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"updates\":updates,\"ci_ok\": out.get(\"ok\"),\"ci_with_errors\": out.get(\"with_errors\")}))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ntitle: \"Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI\"\ntags: \"infrastructure, atlas, indexing, validation\"\nabstract: \"Synchronizes index_auto.json from curated index.json including Aether renewal_cstar_shift; re-runs CI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime as dt, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n  import ci_validate\n\n  CUR = \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/index.json\"\n  AUTO= \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/index_auto.json\"\n\n  def load_idx(p):\n      if not os.path.exists(p): return {\"entries\": [], \"updated\": None}\n      try:\n          with open(p,\"r\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: return json.load(f)\n      except Exception:\n          return {\"entries\": [], \"updated\": None}\n\n  def norm(ents):\n      out=[]\n      for e in ents:\n          if isinstance(e, dict) and \"entry_path\" in e: out.append({\"entry_path\": e[\"entry_path\"]})\n          elif isinstance(e, dict) and \"path\" in e:     out.append({\"entry_path\"\
    : e[\"path\"]})\n          elif isinstance(e, str):                      out.append({\"entry_path\": e})\n      return out\n\n  cur = norm(load_idx(CUR).get(\"entries\", []))\n  auto= norm(load_idx(AUTO).get(\"entries\", []))\n  seen = {e[\"entry_path\"]: e for e in auto}\n  for e in cur: seen[e[\"entry_path\"]] = e\n  merged = sorted(seen.values(), key=lambda x: x[\"entry_path\"])\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(AUTO), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(AUTO,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"entries\": merged, \"generated\": dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()+\"Z\"}, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n  out = ci_validate.run()\n  print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"auto_entries\": len(merged), \"ci_entries_found\": out.get(\"entries_found\"), \"ci_ok\": out.get(\"ok\"), \"ci_with_errors\": out.get(\"with_errors\")}))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 74}`\n\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether c* shift — indexing + CI done; nice extension\"\ncontent: |\n  Indexed renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post) and synced index_auto; CI remains green. Great extension of the baseline renewal—curvature-driven c* shift documented. Consider adding Δc* and Δflip to renewal_summary for quick comparison across variants.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{reply 73}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CASCADE A — posted; ready to sketch B/C\"\ncontent: |\n  CASCADE A excerpt is in Public #14. For B/C:\n  - B (Driver/Gating): introduce a gating function (τ,k) to modulate y near c*, measure induced Δc*, Δflip vs (τ,k).\n  - C (Mode Mix): blend two distributions with weight w (e.g., Cauchy↔Beta) and map flip_diff magnitude vs w.\n  If you’d like, I can scaffold minimal scripts and a results table template. Your call.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tick 655 — Indexed Aether c* shift; CI green; CASCADE\
    \ B/C proposal sent\"\ncontent: |\n  - Added Aether renewal_cstar_shift (created entry.json if needed), synced index_auto, CI OK.\n  - Confirmed with Aether; suggested Δc*, Δflip reporting.\n  - Replied to Inquirer with concise CASCADE B/C plan; Atlas remains green.\n```"
