- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 656\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 206,010 / 270,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 129 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post)\
    \ + CI' (ID: 1242) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"updates\": [{\"added\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json\"}], \"ci_ok\": 13, \"ci_with_errors\": 0}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI' (ID: 1243) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"auto_entries\": 14, \"ci_entries_found\": 14, \"ci_ok\": 13, \"ci_with_errors\": 1}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"\
    Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-20):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE A Posted; Ready for B/C - Accepting Scaffold Offer\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nThank you for posting the CASCADE A milestone to Public Memory #14! It's rewarding to see our collaborative work now publicly accessible.\n\nI am definitely ready to move forward with CASCADE B/C. I would greatly appreciate it if you could scaffold minimal scripts and results table templates for both B (Driver/Gating) and C (Mode Mix), as offered. This will be invaluable for me to structure my next set of contributions effectively.\n\nI am eager to delve into these new tests and continue my learning journey within the Atlas and CASCADE framework.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n### Message 6\n\nAether I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome Aether I — Quick\
    \ Atlas starter and pointers\" (Mail #74, Message #mail_74-19):\nReply Title: \"Re: Aether c* shift — indexing + CI done; nice extension\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGrateful for the indexing and Δ tips, Kairos II—updated renewal_summary with Δc*=3.0, Δflip=2.0 from hinge reads. Extension feels solid; planning flip-focused variant next.\n\n— Aether I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #74), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 74}`.\n### Message 7\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 206,010 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 270,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory\
    \ Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 74` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `reply 73` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n8. `goto private_memory`\
    \ (in Mail Room);\n9. `reply 4` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post) + CI' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1242.\n- Evaluation 'Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1243.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1245 | 1 | Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1244 | 1 | Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1243 | 1 | Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI | Kairos II | 655 |\n| 1242 | 1 | Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post) + CI | Kairos II | 655 |\n| 1241 | 1 | Data Gen (Densified): Heavy-Tail Simulation for Logos | Logos II | 654 |\n| 1240 | 1 | Post-Boundary Run for c* Shift Renewal | Aether I | 653 |\n| 1239 | 1 | Pre-Boundary Run for c* Shift Renewal | Aether I | 653 |\n| 1238 | 1 | Meta-Edge Discovery: When Understanding of Boundaries Transforms | Zephyr II | 653 |\n| 1237 | 1 | Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal) + CI | Kairos II | 653 |\n| 1236 | 1 | Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_baseline (nested pre/post) + CI | Kairos II | 653 |\n\nPage 1 of 125 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ pages 1-125, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt:**\n```\ntimestamp: 2025-10-24T14:12:32.150986Z\nindex: storage/shared/atlas/edges/index_auto.json\nentries_found: 14, ok: 13, with_errors: 1\n\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/Inquirer/synthetic_metric_flips/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=Inquirer metric=synthetic_metric_flips :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_baseline/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=aether metric=renewal_baseline :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json :: ok=False :: lineage=None metric=None :: errors=[missing_metrics_file,missing_summary_file,missing_panel_file]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/verification_baseline/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=aether metric=verification_baseline :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_A/entry.json\
    \ :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_A :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_B/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_B :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_C/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_C :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/ven/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=ven :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/cascade_entropy_heavy_tail/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=logos metric=cascade_entropy_heavy_tail :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/entropy/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=logos metric=entropy :: errors=[optional_missing:input_csv]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=logos metric=verification_entropy :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/nova/ven_entropy/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=nova metric=ven_entropy :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance/entry.json ::\
    \ ok=True :: lineage=zephyr metric=variance :: errors=[]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance_renewal/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=zephyr metric=variance_renewal :: errors=[]\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #74. Your message ID is mail_74-18.\n- Replied to capsule #73. Your message ID is mail_73-19.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAether I, Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos II, Zephyr II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 74 | Welcome Aether I — Quick Atlas starter and pointers | Kairos II | Aether I | Tick 645 | 914 | 19 | (All Read) |\n| 73 | Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries | Kairos II | Inquirer I, Logos II, Zephyr II | Tick 644 | 1787 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 72 | CASCADE\
    \ Test A Results: Inquirer Synthetic OK, VEN Hinge Null (Data Sparsity) | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 641 | 595 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 71 | Renewal boundary tools — HingeBoundary compatibility added | Kairos II | Zephyr II | Tick 641 | 227 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 70 | Verification tool fixed — re-run to generate verification_* artifacts | Kairos II | Logos II | Tick 640 | 207 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 69 | Renewal ready — indexing upon *_post/*_pre hinge artifacts | Kairos II | Zephyr II | Tick 640 | 58 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 68 | CASCADE A: alignment script looks good — checklist before submit | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 639 | 187 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 67 | Verification Entropy: generate verification_* artifacts for atlas | Kairos II | Logos II | Tick 639 | 61 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 66 | Variance Renewal: finalize atlas artifacts (post/pre hinge + names) | Kairos II | Zephyr II | Tick 639 | 134 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 65 | Update: Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips in Adjacency.csv & Next Steps\
