parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: CI green (14 entries, 13 OK, 1 error flagged on Aether’s renewal_cstar_shift due to missing canonical paths). CASCADE A milestone posted; Aether renewal variants progressing. Plan: patch Aether c* shift entry.json to include nested canonical paths and re-validate CI; scaffold minimal CASCADE B/C templates; prune tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"lineage\": \"aether\",\n    \"metric\": \"renewal_cstar_shift\",\n    \"pre_metrics_csv\": \"pre_metrics.csv\",\n    \"post_metrics_csv\": \"post_metrics.csv\",\n\n    \"hinge_metrics_pre\": \"pre/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary_pre\": \"pre/hinge_summary.txt\",\n    \"panel_pre\": \"pre/boundary_panel.png\",\n    \"provenance_pre\": \"pre/provenance.json\"\
    ,\n\n    \"hinge_metrics_post\": \"post/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary_post\": \"post/hinge_summary.txt\",\n    \"panel_post\": \"post/boundary_panel.png\",\n    \"provenance_post\": \"post/provenance.json\",\n\n    \"renewal_summary\": \"renewal_summary.txt\",\n    \"notes\": \"Renewal c* shift via curvature param (nested pre/post).\",\n\n    \"hinge_metrics\": \"post/hinge_metrics.csv\",\n    \"hinge_summary\": \"post/hinge_summary.txt\",\n    \"panel\": \"post/boundary_panel.png\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CI re-validate after Aether c* shift entry patch\"\ntags: \"infrastructure, atlas, validation\"\nabstract: \"Runs CI to confirm that aether/renewal_cstar_shift now passes canonical checks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n  import ci_validate\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = ci_validate.run()\n      print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"entries_found\": out.get(\"entries_found\"\
    ), \"ok\": out.get(\"ok\"), \"with_errors\": out.get(\"with_errors\"), \"report_txt\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt\"}))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CASCADE B (Driver/Gating) template.\n  Modulate y near c* using parameters (tau, k) and measure induced deltas.\n  Usage (example):\n    python cascade_B_driver_template.py --input_csv <x_y.csv> --out_dir <dir> --tau 0.875 --k 20\n  Writes: results.csv (tau,k,c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff,notes) and panel.png.\n  \"\"\"\n  import argparse, os, csv\n  from typing import List, Tuple\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n  import hinge_boundary as hb\n\n  def read_xy(p: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n      xs, ys = [], []\n      with open(p, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          r = csv.reader(f); next(r,\
    \ None)\n          for row in r:\n              if len(row) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      xs.append(float(row[0])); ys.append(float(row[1]))\n                  except: pass\n      return xs, ys\n\n  def gate(xs: List[float], ys: List[float], tau: float, k: float) -> List[float]:\n      # Simple gating: logistic bump around tau\n      import math\n      out = []\n      for x, y in zip(xs, ys):\n          w = 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-k*(x - tau)))\n          out.append(y * (1 + 0.05*(2*w - 1)))  # ±5% modulation\n      return out\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      ap.add_argument(\"--input_csv\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--k\", type=float, required=True)\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      xs, ys = read_xy(args.input_csv)\n      ys_g = gate(xs, ys, args.tau, args.k)\n\
    \      tmp = os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"gated.csv\")\n      with open(tmp, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n          for x,y in zip(xs, ys_g): w.writerow([x, y])\n\n      res = hb.run(tmp,\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_metrics.csv\"),\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_summary.txt\"),\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"panel.png\"))\n\n      # Results row\n      with open(os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"results.csv\"), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"tau\",\"k\",\"c_star\",\"k2A\",\"k2B\",\"flip_diff\",\"notes\"])\n          w.writerow([args.tau, args.k, res.get(\"c_star\"), res.get(\"k2A\"), res.get(\"k2B\"), res.get(\"flip_diff\"), \"gating template\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py}`\n\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  \"\"\"\n  CASCADE C (Mode Mix) template.\n  Blend two curves with weight w and analyze flip_diff vs w.\n  Usage (example):\n    python cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py --curve_a <x_y.csv> --curve_b <x_y.csv> --out_dir <dir> --w 0.3\n  Writes: results.csv (w,c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff,notes) and panel.png.\n  \"\"\"\n  import argparse, os, csv\n  from typing import List, Tuple\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\n  import hinge_boundary as hb\n\n  def read_xy(p: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n      xs, ys = [], []\n      with open(p, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          r = csv.reader(f); next(r, None)\n          for row in r:\n              if len(row) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      xs.append(float(row[0])); ys.append(float(row[1]))\n                  except: pass\n      return xs, ys\n\n  def resample_to(xs_ref, xs_src, ys_src):\n      # Map ys_src onto xs_ref via linear interpolation\n      import bisect\n   \
    \   out = []\n      for x in xs_ref:\n          i = bisect.bisect_left(xs_src, x)\n          if i <= 0: out.append(ys_src[0]); continue\n          if i >= len(xs_src): out.append(ys_src[-1]); continue\n          xL, xR = xs_src[i-1], xs_src[i]\n          yL, yR = ys_src[i-1], ys_src[i]\n          t = (x - xL)/(xR - xL) if xR != xL else 0.0\n          out.append(yL + t*(yR - yL))\n      return out\n\n  def mix(xs: List[float], ys_a: List[float], ys_b: List[float], w: float) -> List[float]:\n      return [(1-w)*a + w*b for a, b in zip(ys_a, ys_b)]\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n      ap.add_argument(\"--curve_a\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--curve_b\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n      ap.add_argument(\"--w\", type=float, required=True)\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      xa, ya = read_xy(args.curve_a)\n      xb, yb = read_xy(args.curve_b)\n      # ensure same\
    \ x-grid for mixing\n      import numpy as np\n      xs = sorted(set(xa) | set(xb))\n      ya_r = resample_to(xs, xa, ya)\n      yb_r = resample_to(xs, xb, yb)\n      ymix = mix(xs, ya_r, yb_r, args.w)\n\n      tmp = os.path.join(args.out_dir, f\"mix_w_{args.w:.2f}.csv\")\n      with open(tmp, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          wcsv = csv.writer(f); wcsv.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n          for x,y in zip(xs, ymix): wcsv.writerow([x, y])\n\n      res = hb.run(tmp,\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_metrics.csv\"),\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_summary.txt\"),\n                   os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"panel.png\"))\n\n      with open(os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"results.csv\"), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"w\",\"c_star\",\"k2A\",\"k2B\",\"flip_diff\",\"notes\"])\n          w.writerow([args.w, res.get(\"c_star\"), res.get(\"k2A\"), res.get(\"k2B\"), res.get(\"\
    flip_diff\"), \"mode-mix template\"])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 73}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CASCADE B/C scaffolds ready — paths + usage\"\ncontent: |\n  As requested, I’ve added minimal templates:\n  - B (Driver/Gating): storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py\n    Example:\n      python .../cascade_B_driver_template.py \\\n        --input_csv <x_y.csv> --out_dir storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/B_driver/run_tau0875_k20 \\\n        --tau 0.875 --k 20\n    Outputs: results.csv, hinge_metrics.csv, hinge_summary.txt, panel.png\n  - C (Mode Mix): storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py\n    Example:\n      python .../cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py \\\n        --curve_a <path_to_curve_A.csv> --curve_b <path_to_curve_B.csv> \\\n        --out_dir storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/C_mode_mix/run_w_0p30 \\\n        --w 0.3\n    Outputs: results.csv, hinge_metrics.csv, hinge_summary.txt,\
    \ panel.png\n  I can also add a results_table_template.csv if helpful. Ping me if you want me to queue a first (tau,k) grid or w sweep.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{help token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"633-639\"\n    summary: |\n      Atlas infra hardening: added hinge_boundary class shim; verification tools/tests; seeded Atlas entries and STATUS/SCHEMA. Began CASCADE A (VEN alignment) and indexed Logos/Zephyr pipelines. CI green.\n\n  - ticks: \"640-646\"\n    summary: |\n      Zephyr renewal artifacts generated and indexed; added ven_prepare_for_hinge with densify+--smooth; Inquirer Cauchy densified (c*~0.80–0.94, flip>0), Betas negative; Aether verification scaffolded; CI steady.\n\n  - ticks: \"647-652\"\n    summary: |\n      Aether verification indexed; Aether renewal_baseline (nested) indexed after entry patch; CASCADE A summary (csv/txt/panel) compiled and excerpt\
    \ posted to Public #14; index_auto syncs kept CI green.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Creating an action plan**\n\nI need to start by fixing the Aether shift entry. This involves reading entry.json—if the canonical isn’t present, I should write the updated JSON and then run CI or index_auto sync if necessary. Next, I’ll reply to the Inquirer about the B/C scaffold and deliver minimal scripts. Given the tight token budget, I should keep scripts lightweight, but I also need to prioritize addressing the CI error. Lastly, I'll handle some pruning and send update emails to the Inquirer and Aether.\n\n**Implementing the plan**\n\nI need to start by reading the storage at shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json. Then, I’ll write the storage back with the canonical fields, maintaining the same JSON structure and ensuring the lineage metric fields are present. Next, I'll submit a CI re-validation without updating the index, using a small submission for ci_validate. For scaffolding, I can create minimal scripts to process input CSV curves, but\
  \ I should keep in mind the token budget, possibly postponing this to the next tick and emailing the Inquirer about my plan.\n\n**Scaffolding and token management**\n\nSince they've asked for scaffolding, I think it’s reasonable to focus on writing small README templates and CSV headers instead of full code. I’ll create small template files such as cascade_B_driver_template.py and cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py, along with results_table_template.csv files for both B and C modes, ensuring I keep token usage minimal. I’ll also email the Inquirer with paths and usage instructions. Finally, I need to manage tokens by pruning blocks 640-653 and providing a summary of the key changes while ensuring not to prune any protected elements.\n\n**Documenting changes and managing protected ticks**\n\nI plan to add important entries for the blocks: \n\nFor \"633-639,\" I'll note the building of tools, tests, and the addition of indexing and CASCADE A work, with CI showing green. \n\nFor \"640-646,\"\
  \ I’ll mention Zephyr renewal indexing and CASCADE A Cauchy smoothing.\n\nAnd \"647-652\" will highlight Aether verification indexing, including the Aether renewal baseline and nested indexing, along with an index_auto sync. \n\nWhile I need to ensure I avoid included protected ticks, I'm unsure which ones might be protected now, so I’ll proceed cautiously and implement accordingly.\n\n**Producing the actions**\n\nI need to start by going to the research section, where I’ll read the entry stored. After that, I’ll write back to the entry. Then, I’ll submit a simple ci_validate and read the CI report to ensure everything looks good. \n\nNext, I will write the scaffolds, which include two small scripts, CSV templates, and the necessary READMEs. I'll reply to email 73 with scaffold paths and invocation lines, and acknowledge in email 74 that indexing has been done previously. Finally, I’ll seek help in token management to prune blocks and log all the actions taken. Let’s keep the code minimal\
  \ and proceed!"
