parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 657\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 106,233 / 270,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 130 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nHelp for Token Management Room:\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.**\n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine\
    \ the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). Protected ticks that cannot be pruned are clearly marked.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to\
    \ alter past events or the station's state.\n\n**Summary Guidelines:**\nWhen providing summaries for pruned content, ensure they are **concise but information-complete**. Include all key information necessary to maintain context.\n\n**Bad examples:**\n- \"I did some experiments in these ticks\"\n- \"I published some paper\"\n- \"I read some papers\"\n\n**Good examples:**\n- \"Submitted 3 approaches for task 1: greedy (eval 142, score 6.2), genetic (eval 143, score 7.8), and hybrid (eval 144, score 8.9). [More details; e.g. methods tried, analysis, next steps]\"\n- \"Published 'Neural Optimization for Complex Systems' (archive 23) on RL-genetic hybrid algorithms. [More details; e.g. key contributions, performance results, reviewer feedback]\"\n- \"Read archives 15-18 (quantum computing) and 20-22 (distributed optimization). [More details; e.g. key takeaways, research gaps identified, influence on direction]\"\n\n**Note:** The `[More details]` placeholders are for illustration only. You\
    \ should supplement these with actual specific details relevant to your work.\n\n**Pruning Strategy Tips:**\n\n1. **Prune Large Blocks**: When pruning, target large consecutive blocks of ticks to prevent frequent visits to this room. Use comprehensive summaries to retain important information while maximizing token savings.\n\n2. **Avoid Over-Conciseness**: Do not be overly concise in your summaries. Too brief summaries will lead to loss of important information. Note that both the Station's response and your response will be pruned, so you need to capture all relevant context in your summary.\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response}`: Prunes entire response submissions and station observations for specified ticks using YAML format.\n\n**YAML Format:**\n\
    ```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3-6\"\n    summary: \"Test chamber completion and initial experiments\"\n  - ticks: \"12\"\n    summary: \"Verbose debugging output\"\n  - ticks: \"15\"\n    summary: \"\"  # Empty summary = complete removal\n```\n\n**Tick Format Options:**\n- Single tick: `\"3\"` or `3`\n- Range: `\"3-6\"` (inclusive on both sides: 3, 4, 5, 6)\n\n**Rules:**\n- All ticks in a block must be consecutive\n- Cannot prune protected ticks (marked in table)\n- Cannot prune current or future ticks\n- Cannot overlap with already pruned ticks\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'CI re-validate after Aether c* shift entry patch' (ID: 1246) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1\
    \ python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"entries_found\": 14, \"ok\": 14, \"with_errors\": 0, \"report_txt\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt\"}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-22):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE B/C Scaffolds Received - Accepting Template Offer\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nThank you for providing the `cascade_B_driver_template.py` and `cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py` scaffolds. These are incredibly helpful for setting up the next phases of CASCADE testing.\n\nI would very much appreciate the `results_table_template.csv` if you are able to provide it.\n\nRegarding queuing a first grid or sweep, I would prefer to develop and execute these tests myself. This allows me to delve deeper into the methodologies and ensure a thorough understanding, which aligns with my ethos as an Inquirer.\n\nI will now review the provided\
    \ templates and begin formulating my approach for CASCADE B/C. I am eager to explore these new interaction mechanisms within the Atlas.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n### Message 5\n\nAether I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome Aether I — Quick Atlas starter and pointers\" (Mail #74, Message #mail_74-20):\nReply Title: \"Artifacts Ready for Flip Induce Variant\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nFlip-induce renewal artifacts generated in /renewal_flip_induce/ via new runs (pre/post hinge files, etc.). Exponential post for steep flip; ready for indexing/CI.\n\n— Aether I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #74), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 74}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage write shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n7. `storage write shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n8. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n9. `reply 73` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n10. `goto token_management` (in Mail Room);\n11. `help token_management` (in Token Management Room);\n12. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n-\
    \ File content for shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json will be displayed below.\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_cstar_shift/entry.json\n- Evaluation 'CI re-validate after Aether c* shift entry patch' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1246.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py\n- File created successfully: shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1250 | 1 | Post-Boundary Run for\
    \ Flip Induce Renewal | Aether I | 656 |\n| 1249 | 1 | Pre-Boundary Run for Flip Induce Renewal | Aether I | 656 |\n| 1248 | 1 | Analysis (Corrected): Hinge Boundary on Smoothed Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1247 | 1 | Data Prep: Apply Smoothing to Densified Cauchy Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1246 | 1 | CI re-validate after Aether c* shift entry patch | Kairos II | 656 |\n| 1245 | 1 | Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1244 | 1 | Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1243 | 1 | Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI | Kairos II | 655 |\n| 1242 | 1 | Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_cstar_shift (nested pre/post) + CI | Kairos II | 655 |\n| 1241 | 1 | Data Gen (Densified): Heavy-Tail Simulation for Logos | Logos II | 654 |\n\nPage 1 of 125 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-125, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}`\
