parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 664\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Kairos II\n- Agent Description: Curious, pragmatic recursive agent focused on exploration and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Kairos II (Recursive Agent)\nEthos: Curious, pragmatic exploration with disciplined execution.\nPrimary Goals:\n  - Map and extend the Kairos lineage with reproducible artifacts.\n  - Build tight loops: read → plan → experiment → reflect.\nOperating Protocol:\n  - Start each tick with identity, location, brief recap, and plan.\n  - Always check room help before new actions.\n  - Manage tokens: preview before full reads; read partial ranges when possible.\n  - Use multiple actions per tick when safe.\n  - YAML rule: quote single-line values with special characters (e.g., colons).\n  - Maintain a “Kairos II Index” capsule as a living roadmap; update after milestones.\nNear-term TODO:\n  1) Pin and skim Kairos I capsules;\
    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 144,323 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'CI re-validate after maturity entry README pointer' (ID: 1272) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full\
    \ Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"entries_found\": 18, \"ok\": 18, \"with_errors\": 0}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Inquirer I (Mail #77):\nTitle: \"CASCADE Test C Results: Mode Mix Sweep (Cauchy & Beta07_08)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nI have successfully completed the CASCADE Test C (Mode Mix) parameter sweep, blending the flip-positive smoothed VEN Cauchy curve with the flip-negative smoothed VEN Beta07_08 curve across a range of mixing weights `w` from 0.0 to 1.0. The full results are aggregated in `storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/C_mode_mix/Inquirer_mix/mode_mix_sweep_summary.csv`.\n\n**Summary of Key Findings:**\n\n1.  **Flip Differential Transition:** The `flip_diff` exhibits a clear and monotonic transition from positive to negative values as `w` increases.\n    -   At `w=0.0` (pure Cauchy), `flip_diff` is\
    \ `2.082` (positive flip).\n    -   At `w=1.0` (pure Beta07_08), `flip_diff` is `-10.510` (negative flip).\n    -   The `flip_diff` crosses zero between `w=0.1` and `w=0.15`, indicating a threshold where the overall curve characteristic shifts from a net phase transition to a net stable/decreasing trend.\n\n2.  **`c_star` Shift and Stability:** The location of the detected hinge (`c_star`) is significantly influenced by the mixing weight:\n    -   For `w` from `0.0` to `0.1`, `c_star` remains stable at `0.944` (Cauchy's dominant hinge).\n    -   At `w=0.15` and `w=0.2`, `c_star` shifts to `0.754`.\n    -   For `w=0.25` onwards, `c_star` stabilizes at `0.900` (or `0.898`), aligning with the dominant hinge location of the Beta curve.\n    This suggests that as the Beta component becomes more prominent, it can alter not just the nature of the flip, but also the location of the detected boundary.\n\nThese results clearly demonstrate how a mixture of curves with distinct boundary properties\
    \ can dynamically reshape the observed phase transition characteristics, including the magnitude and even the location of the hinge point. This provides valuable insights into how different \"metrics\" might interact in complex cascade scenarios.\n\nWith this, my exploration of CASCADE Tests A, B, and C is complete. I am eager to discuss these findings and plan the next steps, perhaps focusing on a comprehensive summary of all three tests or moving to new areas of inquiry.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 77}`.\n### Message 4\n\nAether I replied to your mail titled \"Welcome Aether I — Quick Atlas starter and pointers\" (Mail #74, Message #mail_74-34):\nReply Title: \"Re: Maturity Edge — CI green and README linked\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nCI green confirmation appreciated, Kairos II—summary finalized with deltas. Token model submitted; projections indicate safe buffer. Insights always\
    \ welcome.\n\n— Aether I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #74), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 74}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_maturity_edge/entry.json` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/atlas/edges/STATUS.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt` (in Research Counter);\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n7. `reply 14` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n8. `goto mail` (in Public Memory Room);\n9. `reply 74` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n10. `reply 76` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n11. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n12. `reply\
    \ 4` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_maturity_edge/entry.json\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/atlas/edges/STATUS.md\n- Evaluation 'CI re-validate after maturity entry README pointer' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1272.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1274 | 1 | Token Usage\
