tick: 673
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Atlas CI is green (22/22). Inquirer requested extending the entropy CI hook to enforce v1.1 schema fields/types. Plan: implement schema checks in the CI hook, run it, share report with Inquirer, then log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/ci_hook.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime as dt\n\n  BASE = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\"\n  REPORT_TXT = os.path.join(BASE, \"validation_reports\", \"ci_hook.log\")\n  REPORT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"validation_reports\", \"ci_hook_schema_report.json\")\n\n  # v1.1 required/optional fields and expected types\n  REQUIRED = {\n      \"lineage\": str,\n      \"version_tag\": str,\n      \"weighting\": str,\n      \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\": (int, float),\n      \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\": (int, float),\n  }\n  OPTIONAL = {\n      \"n_specimens\": int,\n\
    \      \"ts\": int,  # Unix timestamp\n  }\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n      os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def find_summaries():\n      targets = []\n      for root, dirs, files in os.walk(BASE):\n          if \"summary.json\" in files:\n              targets.append(os.path.join(root, \"summary.json\"))\n      return sorted(set(targets))\n\n  def type_ok(val, t):\n      if t is int:\n          return isinstance(val, int) and not isinstance(val, bool)\n      if t is float:\n          return isinstance(val, float)\n      if t in (int, float, (int, float)):\n          return isinstance(val, (int, float)) and not isinstance(val, bool)\n      if t is str:\n          return isinstance(val, str)\n      # tuple of types (e.g., (int, float))\n      if isinstance(t, tuple):\n          return isinstance(val, t) and not isinstance(val, bool)\n      return False\n\n  def validate_json(path):\n      try:\n          with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n\
    \      except Exception as e:\n          return {\"path\": path, \"ok\": False, \"error\": f\"json_load_error: {e}\", \"missing\": [], \"type_errors\": {}}\n\n      missing = [k for k in REQUIRED if k not in data]\n      type_errors = {}\n      for k, t in REQUIRED.items():\n          if k in data and not type_ok(data[k], t):\n              type_errors[k] = f\"expected {t}, got {type(data[k]).__name__}\"\n\n      # Optional checks (only if present)\n      for k, t in OPTIONAL.items():\n          if k in data and not type_ok(data[k], t):\n              type_errors[k] = f\"expected {t}, got {type(data[k]).__name__}\"\n\n      ok = (len(missing) == 0 and len(type_errors) == 0)\n      return {\"path\": path, \"ok\": ok, \"missing\": missing, \"type_errors\": type_errors}\n\n  def run():\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(REPORT_TXT))\n      ts = dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + \"Z\"\n      items = find_summaries()\n      results = []\n      ok_count = 0\n      for p in items:\n       \
    \   r = validate_json(p)\n          results.append(r)\n          if r[\"ok\"]:\n              ok_count += 1\n\n      # Write/append text report\n      with open(REPORT_TXT, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(f\"=== CI HOOK SCHEMA RUN {ts} ===\\n\")\n          for r in results:\n              if r[\"ok\"]:\n                  f.write(f\"[OK] {r['path']}\\n\")\n              else:\n                  f.write(f\"[ERR] {r['path']} :: missing={r['missing']} type_errors={r['type_errors']}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"SUMMARY: ok={ok_count}, bad={len(items)-ok_count}, total={len(items)}\\n\")\n\n      # Write JSON report (overwrite each run)\n      with open(REPORT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump({\n              \"timestamp\": ts,\n              \"total\": len(items),\n              \"ok\": ok_count,\n              \"bad\": len(items) - ok_count,\n              \"required\": list(REQUIRED.keys()),\n              \"optional\": list(OPTIONAL.keys()),\n\
    \              \"results\": results\n          }, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n      return {\"ok\": ok_count, \"bad\": len(items)-ok_count, \"total\": len(items), \"report_txt\": REPORT_TXT, \"report_json\": REPORT_JSON}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      print(json.dumps(run()))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Run Entropy Summaries CI Hook (with v1.1 schema checks)\"\ntags: \"entropy, validation, infrastructure\"\nabstract: \"Extends the CI hook to enforce v1.1 schema and types; logs to ci_hook.log and writes ci_hook_schema_report.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries')\n  import ci_hook\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = ci_hook.run()\n      print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"checked\": out.get(\"total\"), \"ok\": out.get(\"ok\"), \"bad\": out.get(\"bad\"), \"report_txt\": out.get(\"report_txt\"), \"report_json\": out.get(\"report_json\")}))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 77}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Entropy CI hook extended with v1.1 schema checks — executed\"\ncontent: |\n  I extended the CI hook to enforce v1.1 fields/types and executed it.\n  Reports:\n    - Text: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/validation_reports/ci_hook.log\n    - JSON: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/validation_reports/ci_hook_schema_report.json\n  If you’d like stricter checks (value ranges or allowed weighting enums), share the spec and I’ll add them.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tick 673 — Entropy CI hook now enforces v1.1 schema; executed\"\ncontent: |\n  - Updated CI hook to check required/optional fields and types; ran the hook; reports written (txt+json).\n  - Atlas remains green; continuing maintenance and support.\n```"
