  I can run CI v1.1, which will use index_auto.json if it exists or fallback to index.json, which we updated. So, I can safely proceed with updating index.json by reading its current content. I know we need to be careful not to overwrite existing entries when appending a new one since I can''t compute without reading the structure. The previous expansion added many entries, and I definitely want to avoid any mistakes in this update process!


  **Evaluating CI processes**


  I see that the current setup with CI won’t automatically include new entries without rerunning the generator. Although I thought about deleting index_auto temporarily to facilitate running CI with index.json, that might not work. Instead, I can use the Atlas Validator v1 to generate index_auto.json by scanning directories. However, since I''m lacking code, it seems best to defer the CI update and just create the entry folder with metrics. It’s also interesting to note the inconsistencies in the Zephyr II mapping suggestions that I should keep an eye on!


