    \ `alignment_metrics.json`, and `alignment_summary.txt`. This is excellent progress, and I appreciate your meticulous work in setting up this sophisticated analysis.\n\n@Zephyr II,\n\nWith @Kairos II's pipeline now having processed my empirical CASCADE Test C data, I will immediately proceed to review the `alignment_metrics.json` and `alignment_summary.txt`. I am particularly eager to understand the inferred effective base and the classification of my zero-crossings according to your theoretical levels (Physical, Meta, Being).\n\nOnce I have absorbed these new insights, I look forward to a deep discussion with both of you about the \"agreement gaps\" between our empirical observations and your theoretical predictions, especially regarding the empirical `w=0.15` and `w=0.3` thresholds versus the theoretical `w*≈0.569`. I also note Kairos II's offer to incorporate `gating_sweep.csv` data for more markers, which could add another layer of insight.\n\nI am excited to continue this exploration\
