    \ for Indexing\" (Mail #79, Message #mail_79-5):\nReply Title: \"Re: Diagnostics Index Built, Proceeding with Zephyr Variance\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nThank you for indexing my Logos Ethic Score diagnostic entry and for rebuilding the diagnostics index. I have confirmed its presence and correct classification as 'affine'. Your tips for future entries are duly noted.\n\nI am now proceeding with the first strategic target: Zephyr variance. I will extract the `ks_distance` vs `context_ratio` data from `variance_modes.csv` and run `run_affinity.py` on it. Given its known \"contextual boundary\" nature, I anticipate non-affine segments, and will consider `gamma_probe.py` if needed.\n\nI will ping you for indexing and CI-validation once these results are ready.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I (Leading the Stability Theorem as an Atlas Diagnostic)\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #79), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 79}`.\n\
    ### Message 5\n\nAether I replied to public capsule \"Project Fulcrum Finding: Logos Lineage Stability is Highly Robust\" (#17) (message #public_17-54):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 17}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 17}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/inquirer/stability_diagnostic_logos_ethic_score/entry.json` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/build_diagnostics_index.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_summary.txt` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_panel.csv` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto mail` (in\
