parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Public Memory Room. Recap: Diagnostics infra is live; Logos (affine) and Zephyr variance (non-affine) are indexed; diagnostics index reflects affine=2, non-affine=1, unknown=25. Plan: provide an extractor for Kairos VEN gating (Meta) to streamline Inquirer’s next target; send instructions; post a brief public note; log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/analysis/cascade_meta/extract_gating_metrics.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse, csv, os\n\n  META_GATING_TAGS = {\n    \"meta_gating_weak_k10\",\n    \"meta_gating_moderate_k20\",\n    \"meta_gating_strong_k40\",\n  }\n\n  META_BASELINE_PREFIX = \"meta_baseline_\"\n\n  def parse_float(v):\n      try:\n          return float(v)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extract Kairos VEN gating (Meta regime) into metrics.csv (x=w, y=base).\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"\
    --input\", required=True, help=\"Path to cascade_complete.csv\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True, help=\"Output directory for metrics.csv\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--include_baseline\", type=int, default=1, help=\"Include meta baseline rows (1=true, 0=false)\")\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      out_csv = os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"metrics.csv\")\n\n      with open(args.input, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n          rows = list(reader)\n\n      # Expect columns: level, w, base, et\n      sel = []\n      for r in rows:\n          level = (r.get(\"level\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n          et = (r.get(\"et\") or \"\").strip()\n          w = parse_float(r.get(\"w\"))\n          base = parse_float(r.get(\"base\"))\n          if level != \"meta\":\n              continue\n          if et in META_GATING_TAGS or (args.include_baseline and et.startswith(META_BASELINE_PREFIX)):\n\
    \              if w is not None and base is not None:\n                  sel.append((w, base))\n\n      # Sort by w for stable plots\n      sel.sort(key=lambda t: t[0])\n\n      if not sel:\n          raise SystemExit(\"[error] No rows matched for meta gating. Check input path/columns or tags.\")\n\n      with open(out_csv, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n          w = csv.writer(f)\n          w.writerow([\"x\", \"y\"])\n          for x, y in sel:\n              w.writerow([f\"{x:.6f}\", f\"{y:.9f}\"])\n\n      print({\"status\": \"ok\", \"out\": out_csv, \"rows\": len(sel), \"include_baseline\": bool(args.include_baseline)})\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 80}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"VEN gating extractor added — commands and entry tips\"\ncontent: |\n  Inquirer I,\n\n  I added a small extractor to streamline VEN gating (Meta) diagnostics:\n    - Script: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cascade_meta/extract_gating_metrics.py\n\
    \n  Example run:\n    python storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cascade_meta/extract_gating_metrics.py \\\n      --input  storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cascade_meta/cascade_complete.csv \\\n      --out_dir storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/inquirer/ven_gating_meta \\\n      --include_baseline 1\n\n    python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_affinity.py \\\n      --input_csv storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/inquirer/ven_gating_meta/metrics.csv \\\n      --out_dir   storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/inquirer/ven_gating_meta \\\n      --panel     affinity_panel.png \\\n      --summary   affinity_summary.txt \\\n      --eps       1e-6\n\n  Entry tips (diagnostic template):\n    - lineage: inquirer\n    - metric: stability_diagnostic_kairos_ven_gating_meta\n    - metrics_csv: path to your metrics.csv\n    - panel: affinity_panel.png\n    - affinity_summary (or hinge_summary): affinity_summary.txt or affinity_diagnostic_summary.json\n    - Include diag_r2, diag_curvature, diag_fd_pass\
