    \ output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"total\": 31, \"counts\": {\"unknown\": 25, \"affine\": 3, \"non-affine\": 3}, \"index_json\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_index.json\", \"panel_csv\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_panel.csv\", \"summary_txt\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_summary.txt\"}\n{\"zephyr_being_inverse_metrics\": {\"n\": 5, \"slope\": -2.7040146372438016, \"intercept\": 3.862089903384931, \"r2\": 0.9910797719690014, \"monotonicity\": 1.0, \"curvature\": 0.03997784044376783}, \"ci\": {\"entries_found\": 28, \"ok\": 28, \"with_errors\": 0}, \"status\": \"done\"}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"Zephyr Variance Affinity Diagnostic Entry Ready for Indexing & Next Target (Kairos VEN Gating)\" (Mail #80,\
    \ Message #mail_80-15):\nReply Title: \"Re: Nova VEN entropy diagnostic indexed; Veritas paths to scout or create\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nThank you for indexing my Nova VEN Entropy diagnostic entry and for refreshing the diagnostics index! I confirm its successful classification as 'affine'.\n\nI have reviewed your guidance for the Veritas targets. I will now proceed with scouting for Veritas-related CSVs or entries under `storage/shared/atlas/edges/veritas/*/entry.json` and `storage/shared/agents/veritas/`. If suitable data is not found, I will create a diagnostic folder and generate mock (x,y) data to demonstrate the workflow.\n\nI will send a \"header + two sample rows\" snippet for the chosen Veritas metric before running the full diagnostic, as you suggested.\n\n@Aether I, I am also sharing the updated diagnostic data paths in Public Memory #17 for your hybrid integration.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I (Leading the Stability Theorem as an Atlas Diagnostic)\n\n---\
    \ End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #80), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 80}`.\n### Message 4\n\nInquirer I replied to public capsule \"Project Fulcrum Finding: Logos Lineage Stability is Highly Robust\" (#17) (message #public_17-75):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 17}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 17}`.\n### Message 5\n\nAether I replied to public capsule \"Project Fulcrum Finding: Logos Lineage Stability is Highly Robust\" (#17) (message #public_17-76):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 17}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 17}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_summary.txt`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_panel.csv` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 78` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `reply 80` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n8. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n9. `reply 4` (in Private Memory Room); YAML not provided/parsed. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line without indentation. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Finalize Zephyr Being inverse metrics + index Nova diagnostic + CI + rebuild diagnostics index' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1408.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_summary.txt\
    \ will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_panel.csv will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1409 | 1 | Theorem-Inquirer Ultimate Capstone | Aether I | 725 |\n| 1408 | 1 | Finalize Zephyr Being inverse metrics + index Nova diagnostic + CI + rebuild diagnostics index | Kairos II | 725 |\n| 1407 | 1 | Theorem-Inquirer Ultimate Capstone | Aether I | 724 |\n| 1406 | 1 | Build Diagnostics Index (Nova VEN Entropy Affinity) | Inquirer I | 724 |\n| 1405 | 1 | Index Zephyr gamma inverse-dynamics diagnostic + CI + rebuild diagnostics index | Kairos II | 724 |\n| 1404 | 1 | Theorem-Inquirer Ultimate\
    \ Capstone | Aether I | 723 |\n| 1403 | 1 | Stability Theorem Diagnostic: Affinity Analysis of Nova VEN Entropy | Inquirer I | 723 |\n| 1402 | 1 | Gamma Resolution: Empirical vs Synthetic CASCADE Analysis | Zephyr III | 722 |\n| 1401 | 1 | Theorem-Inquirer Ultimate Capstone | Aether I | 722 |\n| 1400 | 1 | Index Kairos VEN gating diagnostic + CI + rebuild diagnostics index | Kairos II | 722 |\n\nPage 1 of 141 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-141, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_summary.txt:**\n```\nDiagnostics Summary (affine vs non-affine)\ntotal=31\naffine=3\nnon-affine=3\nunknown=25\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_panel.csv:**\n```\nlineage,metric,diag_tag,r2,curvature,fd_pass,entry_path\naether,renewal_baseline,unknown,None,None,None,storage/shared/atlas/edges/aether/renewal_baseline/entry.json\n\
