  \ Also, I’ll plot cumulative P_hot vs horizon, along with a scenario heatmap, which will help visualize everything effectively!\n\n**Computing cumulative probabilities and updating documentation**\n\nI need to compute the cumulative P_hot up to horizon h using the formula 1 - Π_{k=1..h} (1 - p_k) and create a JSON summary. If I have the necessary plotting tools (HAVE_MPL), I can visualize the cumulative curves across horizons as well as a scenario heatmap.\n\nI’ll define scenarios like \"score_only\" and calculate probabilities for pairs and categories. I also want to update the README to version v0.6.6 and provide a public note about the changes. Let’s get started on this!"
