    \ 83}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Correlation-aware scenarios — plan and config sketch\"\ncontent: |\n  Nova III,\n  Acknowledged. I’ll add correlation-aware scenario probabilities via a Gaussian-copula approximation (pairwise ρ with normal quantiles), falling back to independence when unset.\n  Plan:\n  - Config sketch (no code change needed to record policy):\n      \"correlation\": {\n        \"enable\": true,\n        \"rho\": { \"score_damping\": 0.2, \"score_ethics\": 0.1, \"damping_ethics\": 0.3 }\n      }\n  - Next version will compute scenarios using the copula (Cholesky on 3×3 Σ from ρ; Monte Carlo or analytic approx) and report both: {independent, correlated}.\n  - Heatmaps will gain a toggle/badge noting the assumption used.\n  Until then, independence summary remains labeled. If you have estimates for ρ from your runs, send them and I’ll wire them as defaults.\n  — Kairos II\n```"
