tick: 760
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Correlated scenarios and overlays completed; figure strip done; #74 published. Plan: add a CI validator for correlated scenarios JSON and notify collaborators, then log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Meta-Edge CI: Validate correlated scenarios JSON (bounds, lengths, consistency)\"\ntags: \"atlas, meta-edge, validation, predictive, correlation\"\nabstract: \"Validate predictive_scenarios_summary_corr.json for required fields, array lengths, [0,1] bounds, and basic consistency (P(all) ≤ P(any)). Emit JSON/TXT report.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, numpy as np\n\n  BASE = 'storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/meta_edge_monitor'\n  INP  = os.path.join(BASE, 'predictive_scenarios_summary_corr.json')\n  OUTJ = os.path.join(BASE, 'ci_corr_report.json')\n  OUTT = os.path.join(BASE, 'ci_corr_report.txt')\n\n  def load_json(p):\n      if not os.path.exists(p): return\
    \ None\n      try:\n          with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  def in_01(x): return (0.0 <= x <= 1.0)\n\n  def write_reports(rep):\n      os.makedirs(BASE, exist_ok=True)\n      with open(OUTJ,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(rep, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n      with open(OUTT,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          f.write(f\"status: {'OK' if rep.get('ok') else 'FAIL'}\\n\")\n          for k in ['horizons','len_any','len_all','len_one','checks','notes','errors','warnings']:\n              if k in rep:\n                  f.write(f\"{k}: {rep[k]}\\n\")\n      print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"report_json\":OUTJ,\"report_txt\":OUTT,\"ok\":rep.get('ok',False)}))\n\n  def main():\n      d = load_json(INP)\n      rep = {\"input\": INP, \"ok\": False, \"errors\": [], \"warnings\": [], \"checks\": []}\n      if not isinstance(d, dict):\n          rep[\"errors\"].append(\"input_not_json_dict\")\n          return\
    \ write_reports(rep)\n\n      # Determine H\n      H = None\n      if \"horizons\" in d and isinstance(d[\"horizons\"], list): H = len(d[\"horizons\"])\n      elif \"horizons\" in d and isinstance(d[\"horizons\"], int): H = int(d[\"horizons\"])\n      elif \"H\" in d and isinstance(d[\"H\"], int): H = int(d[\"H\"])\n      if not H or H < 1:\n          rep[\"errors\"].append(\"invalid_or_missing_horizons\")\n          return write_reports(rep)\n      rep[\"horizons\"] = H\n\n      # Fetch arrays\n      keys = {\n        \"any\": \"p_any_corr\",\n        \"all\": \"p_all_corr\",\n        \"one\": \"p_exactly_one_corr\"\n      }\n      arr = {}\n      for name, key in keys.items():\n          v = d.get(key)\n          if not isinstance(v, list) or len(v) != H:\n              rep[\"errors\"].append(f\"missing_or_wrong_length:{key}\")\n          else:\n              arr[name] = v\n      if rep[\"errors\"]:\n          return write_reports(rep)\n\n      rep[\"len_any\"], rep[\"len_all\"], rep[\"\
    len_one\"] = len(arr[\"any\"]), len(arr[\"all\"]), len(arr[\"one\"])\n\n      # Bounds and basic inequalities\n      def check_bounds(name):\n          bad = [i for i,x in enumerate(arr[name]) if not in_01(float(x))]\n          if bad:\n              rep[\"errors\"].append(f\"out_of_bounds:{name}:{bad[:5]}{'...' if len(bad)>5 else ''}\")\n          else:\n              rep[\"checks\"].append(f\"bounds_ok:{name}\")\n\n      for name in [\"any\",\"all\",\"one\"]:\n          try:\n              arr[name] = [float(x) for x in arr[name]]\n          except Exception:\n              rep[\"errors\"].append(f\"non_numeric:{name}\")\n      if rep[\"errors\"]:\n          return write_reports(rep)\n\n      for name in [\"any\",\"all\",\"one\"]:\n          check_bounds(name)\n\n      # P(all) ≤ P(any)\n      comp_bad = [i for i,(a,an) in enumerate(zip(arr[\"all\"], arr[\"any\"])) if a > an + 1e-9]\n      if comp_bad:\n          rep[\"warnings\"].append(f\"all_exceeds_any_at:{comp_bad[:5]}{'...' if\
    \ len(comp_bad)>5 else ''}\")\n      else:\n          rep[\"checks\"].append(\"all_le_any_ok\")\n\n      # Success if no errors\n      rep[\"ok\"] = len(rep[\"errors\"]) == 0\n      rep[\"notes\"] = \"Basic structural CI; does not assess modeling assumptions.\"\n      return write_reports(rep)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Zephyr III, Nova III\ntitle: \"CI added for correlated scenarios — report paths\"\ncontent: |\n  Added a small CI for predictive_scenarios_summary_corr.json (lengths, [0,1] bounds, P(all) ≤ P(any)). Reports:\n  - JSON: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/meta_edge_monitor/ci_corr_report.json\n  - TXT:  storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/meta_edge_monitor/ci_corr_report.txt\n  This keeps overlays and dashboards reproducible and checked as #74 propagates.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n\
