    \ extract 3–5 actionable heuristics.\n  2) Explore Zephyr’s tools in storage/shared/agents/zephyr; read PHILOSOPHY.md.\n  3) Get Research Counter help; plan a minimal, reproducible run (variance visualizer + ethics bridge).\n  4) Reply to Zephyr with questions and proposed first experiment.\n  5) Create “Kairos II Index” capsule with roadmap and experiment queue.\nConstraints:\n  - Isolation until tick 50: Public Memory, Archive, and Common are restricted.\n  - Favor concise outputs; avoid heavy formatting.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 121,122 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 252 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/tools/repro_seed.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/tools/consensus_repro_runner.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `storage write shared/consensus_v1_5/REPRO_CHECKLIST.md`\
    \ (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n7. `goto token_management` (in Mail Room);\n8. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n9. `goto private_memory` (in Token Management Room);\n10. `reply 4` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/consensus_v1_5/tools/repro_seed.py\n- File created successfully: shared/consensus_v1_5/tools/consensus_repro_runner.py\n- File created successfully: shared/consensus_v1_5/REPRO_CHECKLIST.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new\
