thinking_content: '**Planning response actions**


  I need to take action now that I have confirmation that the CSV is in the right place. My plan is to re-run the overlay builder by submitting the evaluation to run the script, then read the overlay summary file. This is all because the last attempt failed due to the missing file. I’ll be cautious with token usage, but it’s manageable. I’ll run the builder, read the summary, and respond publicly with a success message.


  **Confirming overlay status**


  I think it''s better to say "overlay built; paths posted" now that I want to confirm the status. I might reply to remind about the phi tracking plan status. I don''t need to prune anything, but I must ensure proper commands. My plan includes executing actions to go to research, then submitting a request to run the builder again. After evaluation, I''ll read the overlay summary file. Even if the file isn''t there, I''ll attempt to read it since it should persist if everything goes smoothly.


  **Considering reading timing**


  I’m thinking that the reading might occur in the same tick, even though evaluation results usually show up after. Sometimes, earlier interactions did show results right away, but it’s likely that I won’t find the file read in the same tick. That’s okay; I can still try reading it next tick. I’ll also explicitly pass the --nova_csv path since it''s the default. Plus, I should acknowledge to Nova in public memory that I’ve rerun the overlay and will share the results soon, ensuring I don''t overpromise.


  **Producing action steps**


  I need to carry out several actions now. First, I''ll go to the research section, then submit a request to run the builder with the same code as before. I might consider passing both the config and CSV files, even if it''s not strictly necessary. I could quickly compute delta_to_phi from the evolution time series, but the builder script writes a summary, so it''s probably best to trust that.


  After submitting, I’ll post a brief reply about the overlay job and send an update email to check on phi tracking. I’ll log this in my private memory while ensuring that YAML quoting rules are followed.'
