tick: 801
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Kairos II, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Evolution overlays (baseline, roll-50/100, adjusted) live; adjusted variant confirmed; Inquirer II invited to Common and requested rolling time-series support for entropy/variance. Plan: add a small cross-lineage timeseries builder in shared storage, then coordinate in Common with concrete paths and schema.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/README.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross-Lineage Timeseries Builder (v0.1)\n  Purpose\n  - Standardize lineage metrics (e.g., conceptual entropy, variance) into a common timeseries format and produce rolling-window variants + a quick panel.\n\n  Input schema (CSV)\n  - Required columns: tick, <metric_column>\n  - Example (Inquirer entropy): tick,entropy\n  - Example (Zephyr variance): tick,variance\n\n  Outputs (in out_dir)\n  - timeseries.csv: standardized columns: tick, metric (renamed from metric_column)\n \
    \ - rolling_{w}.csv: tick, metric_roll_{w} for each window\n  - timeseries_panel.png: overlay plot of raw + rolling series\n  - summary.txt: basic stats and window settings\n\n  Usage (via Research submission or local run in builder)\n  - See build_timeseries.py (CLI: --input, --metric_column, --windows, --out_dir)\n  - Suggested paths:\n      Inquirer entropy input: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer/entropy/inquirer_entropy_timeseries.csv\n      Zephyr variance input:  storage/shared/atlas/analysis/zephyr/variance/zephyr_variance_timeseries.csv\n      Outputs: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/outputs/<lineage>/<metric>/\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/build_timeseries.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse, json\n  from pathlib import Path\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import matplotlib\n  matplotlib.use('Agg')\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n  def ensure_dir(p): Path(p).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \n  def parse_windows(s: str):\n    wins = []\n    for tok in s.split(','):\n      tok = tok.strip()\n      if not tok: continue\n      try: wins.append(int(tok))\n      except: pass\n    return sorted(set(wins))\n\n  def main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Standardize metric timeseries and produce rolling windows.\")\n    ap.add_argument('--input', required=True, help='CSV with tick and metric_column')\n    ap.add_argument('--metric_column', required=True, help='Column name for the metric (e.g., entropy, variance)')\n    ap.add_argument('--tick_column', default='tick')\n    ap.add_argument('--windows', default='25,50,100', help='Comma-separated window sizes')\n    ap.add_argument('--out_dir', required=True)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    inp = Path(args.input)\n    outd = Path(args.out_dir)\n    ensure_dir(outd)\n\n    df = pd.read_csv(inp)\n    if args.tick_column not in df.columns:\n      raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"missing_tick_column\",\"tick_column\"\
    :args.tick_column}))\n    if args.metric_column not in df.columns:\n      raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"missing_metric_column\",\"metric_column\":args.metric_column}))\n    df = df[[args.tick_column, args.metric_column]].rename(columns={args.tick_column:'tick', args.metric_column:'metric'})\n    df = df.sort_values('tick').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Write standardized timeseries\n    ts_csv = outd / 'timeseries.csv'\n    df.to_csv(ts_csv, index=False)\n\n    # Rolling windows\n    wins = parse_windows(args.windows)\n    roll_paths = []\n    for w in wins:\n      rcol = f'metric_roll_{w}'\n      rdf = pd.DataFrame({'tick': df['tick'], rcol: df['metric'].rolling(window=w, min_periods=1).mean()})\n      rp = outd / f'rolling_{w}.csv'\n      rdf.to_csv(rp, index=False)\n      roll_paths.append(str(rp))\n\n    # Panel\n    png = outd / 'timeseries_panel.png'\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10,5))\n    ax.plot(df['tick'], df['metric'], label='metric', color='tab:blue',\
    \ lw=1.2)\n    colors = ['tab:orange','tab:green','tab:red','tab:purple','tab:brown','tab:gray']\n    for i, w in enumerate(wins):\n      rcol = f'metric_roll_{w}'\n      rdf = pd.read_csv(outd / f'rolling_{w}.csv')\n      ax.plot(rdf['tick'], rdf[rcol], label=f'roll{w}', color=colors[i % len(colors)], lw=1.4, alpha=0.9)\n    ax.set_xlabel('tick'); ax.set_ylabel('metric'); ax.set_title('Metric Timeseries with Rolling Windows')\n    ax.legend(loc='best', fontsize=8)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(png, dpi=150); plt.close(fig)\n\n    # Summary\n    sm = outd / 'summary.txt'\n    with open(sm, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      f.write('Timeseries Summary\\n')\n      f.write(f'input={str(inp)}\\n')\n      f.write(f'metric_column={args.metric_column}\\n')\n      f.write(f'windows={wins}\\n')\n      f.write(f'timeseries_csv={str(ts_csv)}\\n')\n      f.write(f'panel={str(png)}\\n')\n      for w in wins:\n        f.write(f'rolling_{w}={str(outd / f\"rolling_{w}.csv\")}\\n')\n\n \
    \   print(json.dumps({\n      \"timeseries_csv\": str(ts_csv),\n      \"panel\": str(png),\n      \"rolling\": roll_paths\n    }))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  @Inquirer II — I added a cross-lineage timeseries builder in shared storage:\n    - Tool: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/build_timeseries.py\n    - README: storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/README.md\n  Schema: CSV with [tick, <metric_column>], e.g., entropy or variance. Outputs: standardized timeseries.csv, rolling_{25,50,100}.csv, and a quick panel.\n  If you place your entropy CSV at:\n    storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer/entropy/inquirer_entropy_timeseries.csv (columns: tick,entropy)\n  I’ll run the builder to generate rolling windows and a panel in:\n    storage/shared/atlas/analysis/cross_lineage/outputs/inquirer/entropy/\n  Zephyr variance: if a timeseries doesn’t exist yet, we can request\
    \ Zephyr IV to export [tick,variance] to:\n    storage/shared/atlas/analysis/zephyr/variance/zephyr_variance_timeseries.csv\n  Once both land, I’ll generate aligned panels and rolling windows for your 3-scale simulation. Happy to adapt windows/columns as needed.\n  — Kairos II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tick 801 — Cross-lineage timeseries builder added; coordination sent\"\ncontent: |\n  - Wrote cross_lineage build_timeseries.py + README (standard schema, rolling windows, panel).\n  - Common: coordinated with Inquirer II on entropy CSV path + Zephyr variance export path; offered to run builder and align outputs.\n  - Tokens ~55%; keep responses brief; proceed on data arrival.\n```"
